{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel","id":1559478,"title":"Game Reasons for the Different Types of Umbral Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-17T07:25:48-07:00","id":1559478,"title":"Game Reasons for the Different Types of Umbral Travel","content":"I have issues with the way Otherworlds travel works in Mage, and I'm considering reworking it. Two big ones are:<br /> <br /> 1) Mage is vague and contradictory about key issues.<br /> <br /> 2) There are seemingly arbitrary difficulties for certain realms, and these are usually handled by heaping on Spheres rather than something more story driven.<br /> <br /> But before I can start addressing those issues, I really need to consider why they are there in the first place. Specifically from a gaming standpoint. To give a prime example: the Underworld. The Shadowlands are sometimes referred to as part of the Penumbra, because they behave like it, right up until a mage wants to visit, at which point they are something else. Mages suddenly need a new method to get there.<br /> <br /> Now we could get into the metaphysics of it, or the publishing history of it, but right now I am more interested in the gaming aspect. What happens if mages can access the Shadowlands as easily as they can access the Penumbra? Does it dramatically change Mage? Also, is the goal here to make the journey more difficult, or to restrict it to more experienced mages?<br /> <br /> I have similar questions about other aspects of Otherworlds mages have difficulty with, such as the deeper parts of the Underworld and the Dreaming in general, so feel free to comment about those as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T08:15:05-07:00","id":1559479,"title":"","content":"Exploration is always a powerful motivation. Mages are the kind of people who need to see &quot;the hill beyond yon hill.&quot; <br /> <br /> Quests are a strong motivation. If a powerful vampire lord is a threat the souls of his mother and father might have secrets that can give your cabal the edge. <br /> <br /> Maybe your group is reforging an ancient artifact. The needed materials aren't found on Earth anymore put it's available in the lands of myth. <br /> <br /> There's always a reason to go on a journey of (self)discovery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T09:36:03-07:00","id":1559484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if mages can access the Shadowlands as easily as they can access the Penumbra? Does it dramatically change Mage? Also, is the goal here to make the journey more difficult, or to restrict it to more experienced mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadowlands are very different from the Penumbra because of crossover elements that are old enough as to have ingrained themselves into the setting. Namely, the typical Umbral sojourn isn't filled with ghosts, nor it's the way you go find them. Nor Ghosts experience the vivid and vibrant Umbrascapes and interact with the spirits there - tho that one could be tackled with Videre shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, <i>summoning and</i> <i>affecting</i> ghosts seems to be much simpler than <i>traveling</i>. So, while I have no idea of what the intent could have been, I imagine that it's mostly to avoid having to deal with a completely different Otherworld that has entire books of his own Lore. Due to these crossover elements, if mages were to access both equally you would have to deal with a more <i>complex </i>Umbra from the get go.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have similar questions about other aspects of Otherworlds mages have difficulty with, such as the deeper parts of the Underworld and the Dreaming in general, so feel free to comment about those as well.\u200b </div> </div> </div>In the case of the deeper parts probably there's also an element of these places being &quot;higher level&quot;, so to speak. That's the same for every game. The deeper you go the more dangerous it gets, so it's reasonable to leave that for more experienced characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T13:41:55-07:00","id":1559488,"title":"","content":"I've suspected as much. The way the Shadowlands were set up in Wraith they are both their own thing and clearly penumbral. Mage meanwhile already has this idea that there is only one Penumbra and the apparent differences in how it looks is mostly to do with viewpoint. These two don't exactly play well together. As you point out, that would make ghosts more prevalent in the Penumbra than we see. The general solution of Mage has been to... well I'm trying to come up with a charitable way of saying this but... to vaguely say it both ways and hope no one notices.<br /> <br /> I really don't think it works well and I have some ideas for how to reconcile it. That's where the gaming aspect comes in. Which idea works the best depends a lot on what the goal is.<br /> <br /> You bring up a good point about overwhelming a typical game with too much Otherworldly travel, I could see that happening if players are too quick to try to jaunt everywhere. My followup question then is how to best handle that. Is the best solution to block mages from going to the Shadowlands until they get powerful enough? Or is it to make it the journey challenging and perilous enough that it isn't taken up lightly? Or something else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T10:13:36-07:00","id":1559526,"title":"","content":"One way to reconcile this is to use the Union's methodology. Each &quot;level&quot; and &quot;section&quot; of the Umbra has a unique vibrational frequency, and going from one to another requires different ways to facilitate this. For instance, the Shadowlands could have a frequency of say (-1,-1) using Cartesian coordinates, while deeper levels of the Underworld would have larger numbers (e.g. -2s for the Tempest and -3/4s for the Labyrinth). Similarly, the Penumbra of the Garou would be more (+1, -1), the Astral Penumbra (+1,+1) and the Near Dreaming (-1,+1), and so on.<br /> <br /> As each level has a different rule set that governs what goes on within, then it stands to reason that each level needs slightly different ways to access. For instance, one must be 'dead' to enter any part of the Underworld. Being temporarily 'dead' counts, as well as being undead such as a vampire. The Garou workaround is to be entirely spirit, which doesn't completely violate the rules. The rules for the Penumbra, and the rest of the Middle Umbra, is that one must have a 'living spark,' as well as a spirit form. This makes it fairly easy for mages and Garou, but vamps need to 'borrow' the spark from something else to enter.<br /> <br /> I've been coming up with a new way for organizing the entire Otherworlds for a while now, and the above just grazes what I've been working on. One day I might post something, but I'm afraid it will just get too big. It includes a few new ideas, plus a different view of the history of the WOD, but it's working out. So far.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T06:24:15-07:00","id":1559532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You bring up a good point about overwhelming a typical game with too much Otherworldly travel, I could see that happening if players are too quick to try to jaunt everywhere. My followup question then is how to best handle that. Is the best solution to block mages from going to the Shadowlands until they get powerful enough? Or is it to make it the journey challenging and perilous enough that it isn't taken up lightly? Or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Making the travel challenging and perilous seems to me the best way to avoid too much layered travel. I think Umbra should feel misterious and very supernatural, full of potential, but also challenges.<br /> <br /> That way &quot;the party&quot; will want to stick together and prepare rather than just portal jump out of convenience. Making the travel it's own adventure.<br /> <br /> But then, I <i>like</i> the Umbra. Both as a player that likes to play very magical wizards, and as a source of plots. So I would rather want people to be able to go there. Making the travel it's own adventure it's its own goal more than a medium. I think RPG should be like that anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T08:49:27-07:00","id":1559582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1559526#post1559526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to reconcile this is to use the Union's methodology. Each &quot;level&quot; and &quot;section&quot; of the Umbra has a unique vibrational frequency, and going from one to another requires different ways to facilitate this. For instance, the Shadowlands could have a frequency of say (-1,-1) using Cartesian coordinates, while deeper levels of the Underworld would have larger numbers (e.g. -2s for the Tempest and -3/4s for the Labyrinth). Similarly, the Penumbra of the Garou would be more (+1, -1), the Astral Penumbra (+1,+1) and the Near Dreaming (-1,+1), and so on.<br /> <br /> As each level has a different rule set that governs what goes on within, then it stands to reason that each level needs slightly different ways to access. For instance, one must be 'dead' to enter any part of the Underworld. Being temporarily 'dead' counts, as well as being undead such as a vampire. The Garou workaround is to be entirely spirit, which doesn't completely violate the rules. The rules for the Penumbra, and the rest of the Middle Umbra, is that one must have a 'living spark,' as well as a spirit form. This makes it fairly easy for mages and Garou, but vamps need to 'borrow' the spark from something else to enter.<br /> <br /> I've been coming up with a new way for organizing the entire Otherworlds for a while now, and the above just grazes what I've been working on. One day I might post something, but I'm afraid it will just get too big. It includes a few new ideas, plus a different view of the history of the WOD, but it's working out. So far.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm leaning towards something similar, with the penumbra especially. Not the cartesian coordinates, but with dropping the idea that the Penumbra is one place. Or rather, dropping the idea that how the Penumbra acts is mostly a matter of viewpoint. Instead there are multiple Penumbral expressions of the same place, say a Shadowlands expression of a house and a more mental (astral) representation of the same house. These might be the same point in a single Penumbra or they might be different Penumbras, mages aren't sure, because getting from one to the other actually requires some kind of travel. Sometimes this is as simple as passing through a door from one to the other or leaving and reentering, other times it is a more complicated and difficult to navigate journey. <br /> <br /> For me this is coming from a project where I'm working on a better writeup of the magic rules which fixes some contradictions and consolidates everything into one place. This does mean getting a better handle on otherworlds travel though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T10:08:46-07:00","id":1559639,"title":"","content":"The coordinates are something I'm working with for my own reimagining of the Umbra. Slight spoiler: It involves three axes, and seven realms in total, with one new one TBD. Oh, and the physical plane is no longer in the center of it all. It makes things so much easier without the human-centric beliefs.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I basically have all the Penumbra layers as reflections of each other. Each one is separate, but equal under the purview of which sector of the Umbra one is in. The mostly means getting rid of much of the personal views as expressed by the Vidiere, but it offers the possibility of keeping every part of the Umbra the same for every splat, with similar rules for each. <br /> <br /> Basically, it's going to take way more time and space than I have here and now to explain everything. My brain runs faster than I can type sometimes, and I'm running fast today. I should really post something of my own soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T12:19:35-07:00","id":1559650,"title":"","content":"Sounds interesting. I look forward to anything you post.<br /> <br /> One thing I've been running into in this writeup is that while the Shadowlands are quite different as a Penumbra, mostly because of their special residents, the astral and spirit wild versions differ mostly in sensory terms. I'd like to have a little bit more character and ecology to them to make them more alive (for lack of a better term). How have you handled that?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-30T09:23:34-07:00","id":1559680,"title":"","content":"So I have two options that I'm looking at with the Penumbra. One is just having separate but constantly intermingling penumbras. The other is using the Periphery to provide a very thin area on the other side of the gauntlet where they all intermingle. M20 uses the Periphery as a purely perceptual thing on the physical side of the gauntlet, but other sources mix it in with the penumbra. Here are the writups I did for them as I was working through the ideas.<br /> <br /> Current way<br /> We have the physical world, then a perceptual Periphery where people start getting senses of the umbra. Then there is the gauntlet and the shroud. Crossing the gauntlet leads to the Penumbra, which is a spiritual realm that looks mostly like the physical world. This is single place that can be seen through lenses corresponding to the high, mid, and low umbras.<br /> <br /> Crossing the Shroud is the Shadowlands, which is a spiritual realm that looks mostly like the physical world. This may or may not be part of the Low Umbra or it may be a second Penumbra. It looks very much like the Penumbra, but it has ghosts.<br /> <br /> From the Penumbra, travellers of the right state can push into the High and Middle Umbras properly. From the Shadowlands, travellers who are dead or dead adjacent can push into (or further into) the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Despite having an area that looks mostly like the physical world, the Dreaming doesn't have a Penumbral Videre or a Penumbra. Anything acting like the Penumbra is fully in the Dreaming.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Prospect #1<br /> We have the physical world, which is separated from the rest by a Gauntlet. Sometimes sensations do seep through. Then there is the Gauntlet/Shroud, which separates the Physical from the Penumbral. There are multiple Penumbras, at least one for each of the four Otherworlds, and it is rumored there are others.<br /> <br /> Travel across the Gauntlet will usually lead to the Penumbra that most resonates with that location in the Physical world and with the crosser's situation. In a Penumbra, travellers can, with effort, see into other Penumbra that have enough connection with the current location. Travel between different Penumbra is possible, though often difficult, unpredictable, or unreliable. It is much easier if the traveller is intending to go to the Penumbra that best matches his state (i.e. Astral Travellers have the easiest time going to the Astral Penumbra).<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are the Penumbra associated with the Underworld. Travellers don't have to be dead or dead adjacent to get there, but it is much easier if they are. The Dreaming also has a Penumbra, though the easiest ways of getting to the Dreaming tend to bypass it.<br /> <br /> Travel into the Otherworlds proper requires being in the Penumbra of the right type and, often, being in the right state. Astral travellers can't push into the Spirit Wilds, and spirit travellers can only get into the Vulgate of the Astral.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Prospect #2<br /> We have the physical world, which is separated from the rest by a Gauntlet. Sometimes sensations do seep through. Then there is the Gauntlet/Shroud, which separates the Physical from the Penumbral. The shallowest layer of the Penumbral is called the Periphery and it is the closest reflection of the physical.<br /> <br /> Travel across the Gauntlet leads to the Periphery. One of the Penumbra will usually influence the look of the Periphery, as will a travellers Videre. From the Periphery travellers can, with effort, see partway into any Penumbras that have enough connection with the current location, though some Penumbra are naturally harder than others. It is difficult to stay within the Periphery unless actively trying, most travel will naturally take the traveller to the most appropriate Penumbra for that location and the travellers state. There are multiple Penumbras, at least one for each of the four Otherworlds, and it is rumored there are others.<br /> <br /> The Shadowlands are the Penumbra associated with the Underworld. Travellers don't have to be dead or dead adjacent to get there, but it is much easier if they are. The Dreaming also has a Penumbra, though the easiest ways of getting to the Dreaming tend to bypass it.<br /> <br /> Travel between different Penumbra is possible, though unreliable. It is much easier if the traveller is intending to go to the Penumbra that best matches his state (i.e. Astral Travellers have the easiest time going to the Astral Penumbra).<br /> <br /> Travel into the Otherworlds proper requires being in the Penumbra of the right type and, often, being in the right state. Astral travellers can't push into the Spirit Wilds, and spirit travellers can only get into the Vulgate of the Astral.<br /> <hr /><br /> The advantage of using the Periphery is it keeps what is just on the other side of the Gauntlet consistent with what we already see. It is, however, more complicated. Thoughts?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T00:58:33-07:00","id":1561558,"title":"","content":"I think you have first to ponder how this affects Paradigm. Among the reasons Mage does this the wonky way it does, is the fact it must let an individual Mage think whatever about how other worlds work and be validated by personal Magic.<br /> <br /> Also, I have to correct you on one thing: the Dreaming does NOT have a Penumbra. There's nothing like it in Changeling.<br /> <br /> Chimerical reality is a superposition over the Material. Chimeras and dream stuff are all around, all the time, at least to some extent in areas that don't have too high Banality. Those things are invisible and intangible to Material beings, but the reverse isn't true. They're fully in the Material.<br /> <br /> So when Changelings interact with each other in Fae form and with weird vehicles, wondrous clothes and whatnot while in an environment like the Material... It is, indeed, the Material, and people passing by will see them, just not as Fae (usually). That's why a Changeling that's fighting a Dragon in a parking lot will appear to a passerby to be playing or hallucinating. The Changeling, their equipment and the Dragon are all in the Material.<br /> <br /> The first level of the Dreaming, the Near Dreaming, already departs from our reality. It can have some geographical correspondence, but it's not much, it looks more like a Middle Umbra Realm that casually maps over Material reality for inter travel purposes.<br /> <br /> My suggestion for the rest is to take a cue from CoD: there's only one Penumbra, but three &quot;Frequencies&quot;. While they interact with the same environment, inhabitants only interact with others in their own frequency. An object or Mage traveler can exist as environment or may narrow to one Frequency.<br /> <br /> Don't think you should limit to which Umbra the traveler goes by default. Instead, passages to them are naturally in their native Frequency only, but supernatural means of travel or detection may be able to bypass this.<br /> <br /> How to integrate the Underworld: put ghosts everywhere. Mage avoided to have much to interact with in the Penumbra because reasons but you can just put them there. The Shroud is the Gauntlet and that's that, their Frequency is the most populated by far as a matter of fact. I don't think traveling further into it should be in fact harder than traveling further anywhere.<br /> <br /> Our last challenge is the Dreaming. It's usually declared a Zone that touch the Umbra all over the place without belonging anywhere. This has a good reason: everyone dreams. But at the same time, the relationship between the Dreaming of Changeling and the dreamscapes of the sleepers has always been muddy...<br /> <br /> What if Dream and Dreaming are not the same place? The Dream Realm is made up of infinite Dreamscapes by the denizens of everywhere, with some pseudo-reality between them made of traveler expectations, artificial inter zones and Dreamscape spillover, all accumulated over time. This is the actual Zone that permeates all other realities.<br /> <br /> From the Dream Realm one can enter the realm of the Dreaming similarly to how one can enter an Umbra from the Penumbra. This is not just a deeper portion of Dream, though. It's the realm of Glamour, a substance related to creativity and some mental states, and inhabited by the Fae. It's relationship to the Dream is intuitive to some, but is actually incidental, I'd say almost arbitrary to those who understand real dreams.<br /> <br /> Your biggest challenge, though, won't be to get any of those to make sense. How to reconcile the Traditional Umbra structure with Everett Volumes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T09:31:53-07:00","id":1561687,"title":"","content":"Changeling is my weak point in all this. That said, I did know that the Chimerical and the Material existed side by side, but I didn\u2019t consider that to preclude there being a Dreaming Penumbra especially when, as you say, there are areas of geographical correspondence in the Near Dreaming. In fact, I\u2019d ask what are the qualities of those regions that keep them from being penumbral? It might help with how to handle Mage and The Dreaming.<br /> <br /> As for Penumbral frequencies, I like the term. This sounds a bit like what I was describing earlier with movement between penumbral vidare (henceforth frequencies) requiring challenge and travel. In particular, using doors and pathways that don\u2019t exist in the physical world and lead back to the same location in a different frequency penumbra.<br /> <br /> Actually, the full idea, which I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve put in this thread was: Accessing a Penumbral Vidare depends on two major elements. The first is location. Every place in the physical world resonates with one (actually more than one) of the penumbral frequencies. Most commonly this is the Spiritus, followed by Astral, then the Mortem, then possibly the Oneiric (maybe going to those correspondences in the Near). Crossing the gauntlet at these points leads to that Penumbra.<br /> <br /> In fact, the same is also true in reverse. The Penumbral frequencies sometimes overlap so some locations in the Penumbra lend themselves to transitioning to a different frequency while others do not, so transitioning between levels often requires journeying to find one of these interference points.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also toying around with the idea that some frequencies have such a dominant connection to the physical that it is much harder to cross back over to the physical from a different frequency. The only problem is this would be best represented by having different frequencies have different gauntlet strengths and that\u2019s more numbers to keep track of.<br /> <br /> The other element is metaphysical state. The above assumes the caster is a standard human/mage, but some creatures and states are far more drawn to one of the frequencies. A ghost, if they could cross the gauntlet, would find that most physical places resonate with the Mortem with only a few resonating with any other frequency, for example. Mages can take advantage of this by changing their metaphysical state. Projecting their minds makes accessing the Astral easier, projecting as ghosts makes the Mortem easier, etc.<br /> <br /> Natural inclination may still play a small role, but it is tiny compared to the former two.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d also point out that while this does assume a Dreaming Penumbra, I considered it to be by far the most difficult to access and would rarely be a reliable way of getting into the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Anyways, that was one idea I\u2019ve been thinking of, and the main reason I hadn\u2019t gone into this yet is it deviates from what Mage laid out: that people in the same place in different Vidare can still see each other. While I don\u2019t like that element of Mage, I want to see what the purpose of it is before I change it.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> As regards the Shadowlands, I never saw any thematic or metaphysical reason why mages should have a hard time getting there. My preference would be to just allow it too. I see a few potential game balance reasons, but I don\u2019t find them that compelling.<br /> <br /> My preference would be that accessing the Shadowlands via standard gauntlet crossing would involve either the effort of finding a time and place where crossing the gauntlet leads to the Shadowlands or making a trek through the Penumbra to get there from another frequency.<br /> <br /> The main alternative is Orpheus style projection, specifically that done by cryopod Sleepers*, which is essentially what the Agama Sojourn is. I\u2019d drop the sphere cost down and use it as a third way of crossing the gauntlet that tends to lead to the Shadowlands primarily.<br /> <br /> *Skimmers appear to be astrally projecting instead.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> For the Dreaming , I was thinking that the easiest ways for mages to access it would be through Lucid Dreaming or Demenses. Whether or not those exist within the Dreaming or just the Dream Zone, they are likely the best jumping off point to the Dreaming as a whole.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Everett Volumes are one of the aspects of Mage I have the least familiarity with. I know they are essentially alternate timelines, but I\u2019d have to go lookup the rest. I\u2019d be inclined to say they exist within the Gauntlet itself, as if the Gauntlet is much bigger from the inside than it appears to be when just crossing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T12:04:07-07:00","id":1561689,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also toying around with the idea that some frequencies have such a dominant connection to the physical that it is much harder to cross back over to the physical from a different frequency. The only problem is this would be best represented by having different frequencies have different gauntlet strengths and that\u2019s more numbers to keep track of.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's the same by another name, instead of different Gauntlet strengths you could replace the table with a general &quot;Affinity Table&quot;, where the standard difficulty to cross over it's 6, and it gets modified by +3 / -3 according to how much or little affinity has the place with the frecuency you're accessing, similar as how many modifiers work in Mage<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyways, that was one idea I\u2019ve been thinking of, and the main reason I hadn\u2019t gone into this yet is it deviates from what Mage laid out: that people in the same place in different Vidare can still see each other. While I don\u2019t like that element of Mage, I want to see what the purpose of it is before I change it. </div> </div> </div>I can't imagine another purpose for this than to keep the &quot;party&quot; together regardless of their Paradigms, as on the Traditions it's likely two mages cross over with different Videres. If it's gona depend on the place or on some sort of &quot;tunning&quot; any mage can do, tho, it can be easily adressed trough this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-14-2026, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-14T13:42:55-07:00","id":1561692,"title":"","content":"I ran into this as part of a crossover game, and settled on something very similar to 'frequencies' with Penumbrae each for high, middle, and low Umbra. Again, this is for a crossover, but the easiest way to make sense of it for me was to<br /> 1) tie Gauntlet strength to the type of Penumbra it borders<br /> 2) let the <i>Essence</i> of the one who steps sideways determine the 'default' Penumbra<br /> <br /> It clicked when I tried to reconcile how Gauntlet strength is different for a Werespider and a Garou, when they nominally enter through the same Gauntlet. The reason is of course because one has Weaver (Pattern) and the other has Wyld (Dynamism) Essence, but that difference makes only sense when they enter the Penumbra through different Gauntlets.<br /> <br /> So why not have a Gauntlet each for three distinct Penumbrae? I didn't see any metaphysical reason why stepping into the high umbra should not be easier in places of mind (Pattern) such at studies, libraries, theaters and so on. And honestly, it feels more consistent when each umbral realm has its own barrier that resonates with one of the Essences. The standard Gauntlet ratings make sense for the Spirit Wilds, but why would the Vulgate be easier to reach from a primal place?<br /> <br /> Dreams are a special case with special rules though. I'm still figuring out how to fit them into this larger picture, but the Essence idea still works to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T09:27:38-07:00","id":1561717,"title":"","content":"One of the things this does it turn the Penumbra into a liminal space, or I suppose I should say, it highlights that it already was one. That actually helps a lot because it gives room for the various Umbra to be their own things.<br /> <br /> Despite my attempts to fit the Dreaming into being a type of Umbra I actually don't like thinking of each of the realms as a different flavors of the same thing. The Penumbra, as an entryway and part of all three made them seem that way. On the other hand, if the Penumbra is a transitory space that exists between all (or at least many) of the various realms, that helps keep them as distinct worlds. <br /> <br /> It also opens the possibility of there being other more esoteric realms that can be accessed that are not part of the big 3 (or 4).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T11:12:34-07:00","id":1561718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561687#post1561687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling is my weak point in all this. That said, I did know that the Chimerical and the Material existed side by side, but I didn\u2019t consider that to preclude there being a Dreaming Penumbra especially when, as you say, there are areas of geographical correspondence in the Near Dreaming. In fact, I\u2019d ask what are the qualities of those regions that keep them from being penumbral? It might help with how to handle Mage and The Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partly my fault, but by &quot;mapping&quot; I only meant it has a spatial relationship when you have a way to cross between.<br /> <br /> Basically, the spatial relationship between Trods is usually similar in both realms. It's also similar if you enter the Dreaming through other means.<br /> <br /> Outside that, though, the Near Dreaming has no resemblance to the Material, unless you count &quot;it kind of pretend to follow natural laws&quot;.<br /> <br /> It can also have several places mapping to the same spatial area, but completely different in the Dreaming, depending only in the Path you follow to reach there.<br /> <br /> You can have a Path to roughly the area of New York, and it leads to a 18th century village full with small green goblins. Another seems to go to the same area, but leads to an Archology all cyberpunkey, but mounted in a living giant apple tree. A third leads to alien ruins in a moonscape that don't really fit any description of the area and has Trods leading to New York, Ankara, the actual Moon and a cave in Antarctica.<br /> <br /> The place is way more Middle Umbra than anything. It's similar to the Material only in the sense of being mostly stable, though sometimes it's &quot;shaken&quot; by Dreamquakes that change the environment completely. <hr /><br /> What I'd suggest about Frequencies is that they're less a &quot;this place&quot; thing and more a &quot;you&quot; thing. All three exist everywhere, but in a given place they'll be more or less populated, have more or less features. Maybe even they do have individual Gauntlet Strengths: it's the same Gauntlet, but the ease to transpose it is frequency-dependant.<br /> <br /> You may add the need for &quot;frequency equalizing&quot; effects for Mages trying to travel to one they're not attuned to, but that wouldn't be a huge thing, I'd put it in Spirit 1: it's part and parcel of being able to perceive them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Magic also probably default to equalizing any target to its own Frequency: if a Verbena uses an effect to carry everyone to the Penumbra, a Mage attuned to the Astral will still travel to the Middle Frequency, as that's the Frequency of the effect.<br /> <br /> The problem with Frequency being a local thing in Mage: it passively challenges the Paradigm of a Mage about the Other Worlds, as it creates independently verified evidence of a specific structure to reality. In Ascension this is a big no.<br /> <br /> It can also be the case that other Frequencies exist, maybe as distillations of the main three. A creature attuned to one of those may face a few differences, which would explain why the Traditions and Garou face a distinct Gauntlet Difficulty from the Technocracy and Ananasi, even when traveling to the same Frequency. <hr /><br /> Everett Volumes are alternate versions of any Realm that may or may not be distinct time lines, and may or may not exist in the proper Realm. Alternate Earths are Everett Volumes, but Zones like the Dream Zone and the Web are also Everett Volumes.<br /> <br /> They're the main unity of Other Dimensions for the Void Engineers, so everything that's not the Conventional Space is an Everett Volume, even if in practice you won't call the &quot;main&quot; volumes of the Umbrae that day to day, would be needlessly confusing.<br /> <br /> Conventional Space for them is the realm of the Enlightened Anthropic Principle, which is a misnomer but whatever. Basically their reasoning goes as that:<br /> <br /> 1. If something has a suitable mathematical model, it exists.<br /> <br /> 2. Living beings, through thought/imagination, add mathematical models to reality.<br /> <br /> 3. Brains are quantum computers, and so most of those models are suitable, hence, they exist.<br /> <br /> 4. The Masses naturally produce the minimum conditions for their existence, forming the base state of the Consensus.<br /> <br /> 5. Whenever something exists that contradicts the Consensus, it's placed in another &quot;reality&quot;. It is actually just existence that is a suitable model, but was rejected by the Consensus.<br /> <br /> From there you can guess that Everett Volumes agglomerate compatible models/existences and shut incompatible ones into other Volumes and so on. And for them, this applies to every reality, all of them being first the leftovers of Conventional Space.<br /> <br /> An important note: since Conventional Space is governed by Consensus, it's only as uniform as Consensus is, so models created in Reality Zones remain if compatible there, and between the First and Second Horizons some Umbrae cease to be distinct dimensions as the models that comprise them become suitable. Beyond the last Horizon there's no Consensus and the extant models are unknowable. Those places can still have Everett Volumes, though.<br /> <br /> Moving to an Everett Volume always requires to cross the Gauntlet, they're aware of it and do account for it normally. <hr /><br /> People in different Vidare see each other because Mage wanted to have the cake and eat it. That's basically a way of saying you see whatever you believe your should see, but won't split the party.<br /> <br /> I think changing it to be a property of the spell achieves the same effect better: you see what you shouldn't, but that's because you got there by the shenanigans of that weirdo, no big deal. <hr /><br /> Jumping from dreams to the Dreaming is already a thing Changelings do, so I agree. Whatever the connection is, it exists and can be exploited without much effort.<br /> <br /> Be it clear, though, that Changelings don't travel in the other direction and don't enter dreams easily. Doing so requires a specific Art and the dreamer to be nearby. When they get out of the dream at the other side, they appear close to the Dream Bubble and there are Paths to other parts of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I don't remember if other Dream Bubbles are visible nearby, but I never saw evidence that this area is really in the Dreaming and never heard of a Path leading there from other places (Paths are not necessarily two-ways).<br /> <br /> So I'd say traveling to the Dreaming through dreams, including Demesnes, is perfectly doable. Just remember that, just like traveling to the Umbra turns you into Ephemera, travel to the Dreaming turns you into Glamour. That's official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T08:16:22-07:00","id":1561823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561718#post1561718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with Frequency being a local thing in Mage: it passively challenges the Paradigm of a Mage about the Other Worlds, as it creates independently verified evidence of a specific structure to reality. In Ascension this is a big no.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I agree at least partially, though I think we need to more clearly state the goal. Because Mage does have specific structures and elements that do seem to exist regardless of paradigm, and this is particularly pronounced in how it handles the Otherworlds. For that matter it has resonance which can infuse an area, so there\u2019s already precedent for some magical actions being easier in some areas.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">So having structure itself isn\u2019t the problem, the problem is making sure there\u2019s still room for paradigm and viewpoint to matter. And having viewpoint be a dominant element of which frequency a mage enters accomplishes that, but it is not the only way. Nor does dropping the important of viewpoint deny it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">I actually don\u2019t think that making frequency depend on location and metaphysical state invalidates paradigms any more than having three to four main otherworlds does. But if we want to apply paradigms to this, other possible ways are that a mage\u2019s paradigm could open up specific actions, places, and resonances that help that type of mage get to a specific frequency.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">From there I agree that for gameplay reasons, if a mage casts a spell to bring multiples over, everyone will end up in the same frequency. I also think that clever uses of consecration or other low rank powers could help mages find each other if they don\u2019t have the means to cross over as a group or in the same place.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Also, for gameplay reasons I think that magically brute force travel into a frequency that doesn\u2019t match location, resonance, or temperament should be harder either in difficulty or in sphere rank. I\u2019m actually partial to sphere rank in this case since I think brute force is actually doing something fundamentally different than using the associations that are already there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">That\u2019s for travel, though. Just seeing and communicating should remain the same sphere ranks and at most have a difficulty spike.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T08:28:55-07:00","id":1561824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561823#post1561823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Also, for gameplay reasons I think that magically brute force travel into a frequency that doesn\u2019t match location, resonance, or temperament should be harder either in difficulty or in sphere rank. I\u2019m actually partial to sphere rank in this case since I think brute force is actually doing something fundamentally different than using the associations that are already there.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mage does tend to tackle this by adding additional Spheres. Which tends to be arbitrary and ain't very elegant<br /> <br /> If the Sphere level needs to change, I would suggest <i>lowering</i> it for matches. Like what Prime did for crafting Wonders. Otherwise traveling it's going to be the province of extremeliy dedicated groups<br /> <br /> I would suggest a higher rank for altering the &quot;match&quot; for the <i>location </i>instead of the individual, to alter travel difficulty for everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:00:13-07:00","id":1561829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561823#post1561823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Also, for gameplay reasons I think that magically brute force travel into a frequency that doesn\u2019t match location, resonance, or temperament should be harder either in difficulty or in sphere rank. I\u2019m actually partial to sphere rank in this case since I think brute force is actually doing something fundamentally different than using the associations that are already there.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally partial to tackling location through differences in Gauntlet rating, but if going through Sphere Rating, I'd say the best option is to lower the requirement to travel to a strongly resonating frequency (both location and Mage are attuned).<br /> <br /> This would lower the threshold for Umbra exploration, which IME is unnecessarily high, and the regular rank would stay as a level where you actually can pierce the Gauntlet as it is supposed to do.<br /> <br /> When neither Mage or place are attuned, you need 1 or 2 extra successes to add attunement to the effect.<br /> <br /> And we get rid of this nonsense of each character hallucinating a distinct environment for really no narrative gain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:16:30-07:00","id":1561831,"title":"","content":"The Umbra should be a vast mystery. Sure, some sections should be mapable but the Umbra as a whole should be beyond understanding. <br /> <br /> The high/middle/low/Dreaming schematic is a minor lifeline in an infinite sea. Yes, catalog what you can, but know it's all beyond your comprehension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T11:28:23-07:00","id":1561832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561831#post1561831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Umbra should be a vast mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>D&amp;D 3rd Edition's <i>Manual of the Planes</i> made the Elemental and Energy planes into infinite masses of pure element with few blobs of foreign matter here and there and alien physics as the Ultimate Source of a fundamental element of your reality should be.<br /> <br /> It was cool as hell. It was also the most unusable version of those realities in the history of the game. Virtually no one used them in play except as generic &quot;dump and forget&quot; magical holes.<br /> <br /> We're not discussing what the Umbrae should Metaphysically be in their entirety, we're discussing how to make the Umbrae a setting element that's coherent enough in how to run it that it facilitates games using it. Which is something the current Videre thingamajig doesn't help with in any stretch of imagination.<br /> <br /> Sure, the concept is cool as hell. But in actual play people avoid it for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T14:35:18-07:00","id":1561848,"title":"","content":"The Dreamtime may be a good case study here. It's Penumbra-like in its behavior, although deviates in some points. But probably the closest we have for a Penumbra of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure we really need to consider Paradigm to establish a connection; Paradigm is, in the end, only a formalized way to express and work with the affinity of Mage and Avatar. That affinity doesn't have to fit neatly into the Essence categories either, imo.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T15:37:56-07:00","id":1561851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561848#post1561848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dreamtime may be a good case study here. It's Penumbra-like in its behavior, although deviates in some points. But probably the closest we have for a Penumbra of the Dreaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not well versed on the WoD's Dreamtime. I have some grasp of the actual Aboriginal <i>Alcheringa</i> of Australia, usually translated as &quot;Dreamtime&quot;, &quot;Dreaming&quot; or &quot;Everywhen&quot; and used as inspiration for the WoD version, but I can say it isn't a Penumbra of the Dreaming and most white people, not to my surprise, misunderstand it considerably.<br /> <br /> Alcheringa (this is but one of the names it's called by the many aboriginal nations) is an extremely complex concept that encompasses an eternal cyclic time that &quot;repeats&quot; itself every day, instructions for land management, moral code, ceremonies and rituals, genealogy, the link between people, animals, land, ancestors and gods, and many other things, also literally mapped through the <i>songlines</i>. It's absolutely linked to reality, and couldn't be farther from a &quot;Dreaming Penumbra&quot;. The translations using &quot;dream&quot; and variations are old and recognized as very unfortunate for causing this very kind of confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T01:46:41-07:00","id":1561880,"title":"","content":"The WOD version is expectedly very removed from the real world concept. There are also quite different perspectives on it from different splats.<br /> <br /> Mage (in <i>Dead Magic II</i>) describes it as &quot;a Shallow Realm created by shamans for their Dreamborn (the term the section uses for spirits) kin&quot;, covering most of Australia. It is distinct from the Dreaming but connected at a higher level, and it also is not the Umbra.<br /> The connection between Dreaming and Dreamtime is described as, and I quote: &quot;Think of them as two different cable channels: [the] Dreaming is MTV, and the Dreamtime is more like the Discovery Channel.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In order to access it, a new initiate needs to be 'attuned' to the realm with a specific Rite, after which they can enter the Dreamtime by stepping sideways with a difficulty depending on location and condition of the practitioner.<br /> <br /> The section also has a Rote and rules to create similar 'Sleeping Lands', areas &quot;between Gauntlet and Umbra&quot;. Overall, the concept is (imo) very similar to a Penumbral realm, especially the Shadowlands. The book directly states that Shallow Realms are a variation of Bastet Den Realms. As with the latter, the main difference to Penumbrae is that they usually do not connect directly to the deeper Umbra.<br /> <br /> The takeaway for the purpose of this thread is that it is a liminal realm that requires attunement to access - different from the usual Essence types - which can provide some rules and mechanisms for Penumbrae that function similarly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T03:51:23-07:00","id":1561885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561880#post1561880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The WOD version is expectedly very removed from the real world concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm opposed to it on moral grounds to begin with, but I don't think it's ideal anyway.<br /> <br /> Rules are the easy part. Mostly we already have them. The challenge is cosmology and metaphysics.<br /> <br /> How would this be connected to the Dreaming within the cosmology taking form here, how would that make particular sense, and what would it solve or add? Why a Penumbra for the Dreaming is needed or useful to the game?<br /> <br /> My impression is that it adds a Penumbra for the sake of it, by appropriating an already problematic cultural concept in a distorted way, without giving enough of a spin to either distinguish it and say it was just inspiration, nor adapt enough to be made relevant.<br /> <br /> Not saying it IS that, just that it's my impression as I can't see the point myself, but I'm open to listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T05:21:46-07:00","id":1561888,"title":"","content":"There is perhaps a misunderstanding, I wasn't suggesting turning the Dreamtime into a Penumbra of the Dreaming. I too think that would be both in poor taste and offensive. I just said that it is (as described in the game) Penumbra-like and the closest thing to a Dreaming Penumbra in the books. I recalled it as an existing concept that was similar to a 'frequency' Penumbra as discussed earlier and mentioned it because I thought it might be useful as a reference. Perhaps looking at Shallow Realms in general instead of the Dreamtime in particular is the better idea here.<br /> <br /> Now, if I were to conceptualize a Dreaming Penumbra following along the outlines of mechanisms in this thread, it would be the 'attuned' Penumbra for Oneiromancers, Dreamfolk, Dreamers, and so on. A place that overlaps with the real world but has daydreams and fantasies fading in and out, and where the landscape shimmers with flashes of what it could become or be. Perhaps the Chimare of dreamers are closer and visible there, too. Its 'Gauntlet' would be weak in places that inspire Glamour and strong in Banal places, while lucid dreams and Demesnes exist as shortcuts.<br /> <br /> Whether something like this would add to the game is of course a question of preference, but I would think so. Separating the Penumbra makes only sense to me if you enrich each with unique options for interaction and character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T06:43:39-07:00","id":1561892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561888#post1561888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, if I were to conceptualize a Dreaming Penumbra following along the outlines of mechanisms in this thread, it would be the 'attuned' Penumbra for Oneiromancers, Dreamfolk, Dreamers, and so on. A place that overlaps with the real world but has daydreams and fantasies fading in and out, and where the landscape shimmers with flashes of what it could become or be. Perhaps the Chimare of dreamers are closer and visible there, too. Its 'Gauntlet' would be weak in places that inspire Glamour and strong in Banal places, while lucid dreams and Demesnes exist as shortcuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is: does that assumes Changeling cosmology? Or is it to replace that completely?<br /> <br /> Because if the idea is to improve while keeping it as compatible with official material for every line as possible, we have a lot of conflict with Changeling here.<br /> <br /> What you're describing already exists in Changeling, sans Demesnes. It's just the Material.<br /> <br /> Chimeras and Dream-Stuff exist all around, occupying Conventional Space, they're just not tangible or visible most of the time. It's a total superposition without Gauntlet, you're solid to them, it's just that they're not solid to you if you are not Enchanted. If you are, you'll perceive the same world around you, but with Chimeras added, and will interact normally with everything.<br /> <br /> Our other question is the Dream Zone, which also has rules in the Umbra, and is where most dreams, and I'm theory Demesnes, reside.<br /> <br /> So, how would this &quot;Shallow Dream&quot; deal with what already exists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T10:10:07-07:00","id":1561898,"title":"","content":"I can give it a shot, but admittedly I'm the least firm with Changeling cosmology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561892#post1561892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is: does that assumes Changeling cosmology? Or is it to replace that completely?<br /> <br /> Because if the idea is to improve while keeping it as compatible with official material for every line as possible, we have a lot of conflict with Changeling here.<br /> <br /> What you're describing already exists in Changeling, sans Demesnes. It's just the Material.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more of a difference in perspective.<br /> Changelings exist naturally in both mundane and Chimerical reality. Chimerical reality is invisible to anyone without Fae-sight. Both realities are separated by the Mists. Because of their dual nature, the Mists affect Changelings differently than others.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of a Mage, this may become:<br /> Changelings exist naturally in both the Material and the Penumbra of the Dreaming. Things in a Penumbra are invisible to anyone without. Both realities are separated by a Gauntlet. Because of their dual nature, Changelings can mostly ignore the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> IMO this changes very little on the Changeling side, but it <i>does </i>make Chimerical reality more accessible for outsiders. Whether this changes anything in the larger picture I don't know- arguably, any supernaturals with an affinity for dreams will eventually find their way into them in the current cosmology as well. The benefit I see with the change is that it provides a smoother transition into the Dreaming for outsiders and adds a liminal realm that would be otherwise missing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561892#post1561892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our other question is the Dream Zone, which also has rules in the Umbra, and is where most dreams, and I'm theory Demesnes, reside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding a Penumbra means there is a new way to access the Zone. Beyond that, I'm not sure it would affect the larger architecture, but maybe I missing something? Demesnes and Chimare could exist both in the Penumbra and the deeper Dreaming at the same time, the Umbra is flexible enough for that.<br /> <br /> Zones in general I think are good candidates for unusual Penumbrae. The Digital Web or the Null Zone come to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T12:21:56-07:00","id":1561904,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> <br /> Excuse me not quoting, the forum is acting up.<br /> <br /> Penumbrae aren't superpositions. It's not just physical beings that ignore the materiality of spirits and objects in them, but also the reverse in all cases.<br /> <br /> There is no contact between realities, and if you can perceive the other side, you're still stuck in your own, still intangible.<br /> <br /> Not with Chimerical substances, which would be actually a more fitting name than reality. If you step in a Chimerical flower or insect, they are crushed. If you move your hands in a way that holds a Chimerical object, you handle it. You're solid for them, all the time, all of them.<br /> <br /> And if you can perceive them, you're in to it, no matter who you are. Enchantment is only the easiest way to notice Chimerical substances. Sometimes drugs do the trick, or other mental states, or being too young. Sometimes mood is enough, though that's rarer. But just by seeing them, they're solid for you. You can touch hold or ride a Chimera. A Chimerical beast can lift you without a Material counterpart, once you can see it.<br /> <br /> Some can lift you regardless. It's rare, but is an effect of some Chimerical substances and forces called Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Mists don't separate anything, that's not their effect. They take memories. To be affected by the Mists is to forget all interaction you ever had with Chimerical substances of any kind, and to have the Mists lifted is to get your memories back.<br /> <br /> Nothing &quot;pierces&quot; or &quot;traverse&quot; the Mists. They are not a &quot;thing&quot;, this is just a name. It's just that when you forget, it's said the Mists have settled in. They're the reason few people talk about fairies even among the supernatural. The Changelings and Chimerae are cosmopolitan, they interact with humans and Prodigals all the time. They're witnessed. They kidnap people at random for weekend parties and return them. Yet no one remembers.<br /> <br /> If a Mage is ever affected by the Mists, they will not just stop seeing the Fae, they'll forget every interaction they ever had. Able to rediscover an interaction happened only through roundabout evidence. A note scribbled will remain, memory gaps can point to something, but the memories are unavailable until a Mind Effect, not Spirit, pierces the Mists. Without this even a memory Effect will fail as the forgetfulness just reassert itself immediately.<br /> <br /> Want to remember without this? You'll need to interact indirectly forever, or find a permanent way to lift the Mists. That won't affect senses, only memory. It's just that if and while you can perceive Chimerical substances, the Mists lift naturally.<br /> <br /> So, there's no Gauntlet. There's really no reality to cross. There's invisibility and forgetfulness of phenomena you actually interact with all the time without noticing. And the difficulty others have to interact with this, aside it being the fact most players know Changeling the least of all lines, is just that it's all counterintuitive. That a typical Mage is <i>precisely</i> trying to pierce reality when they just need to look around with new eyes...<br /> <br /> And a Mind 1 Effect, maybe with Prime 1, to see Glamour. That would give complete ability to interact with Chimerical &quot;Reality&quot;, no other requirement. A stronger Mind Effect would be necessary to hold onto your memories after the Effect is over, rolled against your own rank of Banality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T12:36:21-07:00","id":1561905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561898#post1561898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding a Penumbra means there is a new way to access the Zone. Beyond that, I'm not sure it would affect the larger architecture, but maybe I missing something? Demesnes and Chimare could exist both in the Penumbra and the deeper Dreaming at the same time, the Umbra is flexible enough for that.<br /> <br /> Zones in general I think are good candidates for unusual Penumbrae. The Digital Web or the Null Zone come to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now it decided to just work, figures.<br /> <br /> Zones exist all through the Umbrae, and already in the Penumbra, that's the thing. It's already technically possible to have passages into any Zone in the Penumbra in any Videre.<br /> <br /> The Dream Zone is the most widespread because it touches the Umbra wherever there's something that's dreams, and most everything in the Umbrae dream. In fact, dreaming minds are possibly also passages connecting directly to the Material, which would make this the only Zone, and in fact any Umbral reality to regularly do so.<br /> <br /> I said before, despite the name they Dreaming and the Dream Zone do not seem to be linked more than the Dream Zone and any other place in reality. Changelings have few ways to enter dreams, and they particularly don't involve the Dreaming, even if upon leaving the dream &quot;in the Dream side&quot; they can see Paths/Trods to other parts of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> So, are Dreamscapes just pockets inside the Dreaming, or are they another reality altogether with only loose connections? Sincerely it can't be known for now. Changelings can't notice the difference between realities easily, there are Paths that cross through the Umbrae, and very few Mages have much experience with Dreams through the Dream Zone at all. But as is today, they work perfectly fine and actually smoothly if they're distinct realities indeed.<br /> <br /> Changelings call their reality the Dreaming, but it's actually made out of Glamour, wonder and stories, not unconsciousness and symbols. It's not defined by people sleeping, and if it were it would be rather strange to have high Banality people who dream at all, but that's common and normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T03:03:18-07:00","id":1561922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561904#post1561904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me not quoting, the forum is acting up.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does that sometimes. Logging out and in seems to fix it for me, same as the edit spam detection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561904#post1561904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penumbrae aren't superpositions. It's not just physical beings that ignore the materiality of spirits and objects in them, but also the reverse in all cases.<br /> <br /> There is no contact between realities, and if you can perceive the other side, you're still stuck in your own, still intangible.<br /> <br /> Not with Chimerical substances, which would be actually a more fitting name than reality. If you step in a Chimerical flower or insect, they are crushed. If you move your hands in a way that holds a Chimerical object, you handle it. You're solid for them, all the time, all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree: Contact between realities that bypass a Gauntlet would not be be a unique property for a Dreaming Penumbra. Spirits don't make Gauntlet rolls to exert their Charms on their domains, and it is basically their job to do so. They really only need to do that for manifesting, possession, or otherwise crossing into the Material proper.<br /> <br /> Inverse example: If a gun is fired in the Skinlands and a Wraith in the Shadowlands happens to be in the path of the bullet, the Rule of Ouch applies and damages the Wraith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561904#post1561904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you can perceive them, you're in to it, no matter who you are. Enchantment is only the easiest way to notice Chimerical substances. Sometimes drugs do the trick, or other mental states, or being too young. Sometimes mood is enough, though that's rarer. But just by seeing them, they're solid for you. You can touch hold or ride a Chimera. A Chimerical beast can lift you without a Material counterpart, once you can see it.<br /> <br /> Some can lift you regardless. It's rare, but is an effect of some Chimerical substances and forces called Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>While using drugs, meditation, fasting or other ways to enter an altered state of mind are a common way to perceive Spirits or Wraiths as well, seeing = solid <i>is</i> a unique property. However, it could be explained with that the person able to see Chimeras has actually crossed the Gauntlet. If we're using the frequency model, you could say perception equals a state of harmonic resonance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561904#post1561904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bFinally, the Mists don't separate anything, that's not their effect. They take memories. To be affected by the Mists is to forget all interaction you ever had with Chimerical substances of any kind, and to have the Mists lifted is to get your memories back.<br /> <br /> Nothing &quot;pierces&quot; or &quot;traverse&quot; the Mists.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> So, there's no Gauntlet. There's really no reality to cross. There's invisibility and forgetfulness of phenomena you actually interact with all the time without noticing. And the difficulty others have to interact with this, aside it being the fact most players know Changeling the least of all lines, is just that it's all counterintuitive. That a typical Mage is <i>precisely</i> trying to pierce reality when they just need to look around with new eyes...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I was constructing an alternate version which <i>has </i>a Gauntlet. I don't think that is possible without adjusting at least a few things. I picked the Mists because they were created as a way to protect the Dreaming from Banality, extending their function to an actual barrier in Banal places seemed the least invasive.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561905#post1561905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said before, despite the name the Dreaming and the Dream Zone do not seem to be linked more than the Dream Zone and any other place in reality. Changelings have few ways to enter dreams, and they particularly don't involve the Dreaming, even if upon leaving the dream &quot;in the Dream side&quot; they can see Paths/Trods to other parts of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> So, are Dreamscapes just pockets inside the Dreaming, or are they another reality altogether with only loose connections? Sincerely it can't be known for now. Changelings can't notice the difference between realities easily, there are Paths that cross through the Umbrae, and very few Mages have much experience with Dreams through the Dream Zone at all. But as is today, they work perfectly fine and actually smoothly if they're distinct realities indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember talking about this with you and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> in the WtA forum, and I like the summary in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1555159-entering-and-altering-chimares?p=1555431#post1555431\">this post</a>. I'm still not seeing how adding a Penumbra would collapse or severely hurt the architecture, as the distinction between Dream Zone and Dreaming happens deeper 'inside'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T03:32:27-07:00","id":1561924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561922#post1561922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not seeing how adding a Penumbra would collapse or severely hurt the architecture, as the distinction between Dream Zone and Dreaming happens deeper 'inside'.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not what I asked.<br /> <br /> Why? What do we gain with it? That's what bugs me.<br /> <br /> I know it's possible to adapt everything to add a Penumbra, and to work it in a way that don't change anything. But what does it add besides mirroring the others?<br /> <br /> You said this would make the Dreaming more accessible. It would not: the Dreaming isn't just perceived, it's fully accessible with Mind 1 if you know what to look for. It's counterintuitive, which is in tune with the expected mystery of the place as described in that post you linked.<br /> <br /> Adding a Penumbra cranks the requisite up to Spirit 3, 2 if you want to be generous. Mind 1 if you go out of your way to explain a Penumbra doing what Chimerical substance already did.<br /> <br /> Chimeras don't influence the Material or follow the Rule of Ouch. They treat the Material as a perfectly solid reality. No fuzzy perception, no softer contact, no nothing. They're invisible and that's it. No &quot;the bullet hurt because I believe it should&quot;, but &quot;the bullet hurt because I got shot with a frigging bullet&quot;.<br /> <br /> How a person that traversed to the Penumbra remains visible and tangible in the Material? It's certainly doable to make a Penumbra that will preserve all those properties, but you'll spend a lot of words explaining how this Penumbra is like that and... Why?<br /> <br /> Don't want to know how to adapt the Dreaming to have a Penumbra. My question is why bother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T04:08:21-07:00","id":1561925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561924#post1561924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not what I asked.<br /> <br /> Why? What do we gain with it? That's what bugs me.<br /> <br /> I know it's possible to adapt everything to add a Penumbra, and to work it in a way that don't change anything. But what does it add besides mirroring the others?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I thought the thread topic was to explore the possibilities of a more harmonious architecture that has distinct Penumbrae, and the Dreaming came up as a realm that would need adaptation to fit in with that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1559582#post1559582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm leaning towards something similar, with the penumbra especially. Not the cartesian coordinates, but with dropping the idea that the Penumbra is one place. Or rather, dropping the idea that how the Penumbra acts is mostly a matter of viewpoint. Instead there are multiple Penumbral expressions of the same place, say a Shadowlands expression of a house and a more mental (astral) representation of the same house. These might be the same point in a single Penumbra or they might be different Penumbras, mages aren't sure, because getting from one to the other actually requires some kind of travel. Sometimes this is as simple as passing through a door from one to the other or leaving and reentering, other times it is a more complicated and difficult to navigate journey.<br /> <br /> For me this is coming from a project where I'm working on a better writeup of the magic rules which fixes some contradictions and consolidates everything into one place. This does mean getting a better handle on otherworlds travel though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's fine if you don't agree that it is a satisfying solution. I also enjoy discussing an idea to sort out the kinks, but I feel it is exhausted when the disagreement is back to the initial premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T04:29:47-07:00","id":1561927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1561925#post1561925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because I thought the thread topic was to explore the possibilities of a more harmonious architecture that has distinct Penumbrae, and the Dreaming came up as a realm that would need adaptation to fit in with that:</div> </div> </div> </div>It was meant for a more clear architecture, that is easier to implement in game, at least as far as I can tell. And Ramnesis thought the Dreaming had a Penumbra, or something best described as such.<br /> <br /> My understanding is that exploring other possible Umbrae or actual problems with inconsistency or ambiguity in their depiction that harm actual play as the Videre did is more conducive of forward discussion now.<br /> <br /> The Far and Deep Dreaming can, in fact, fit the bill, as I think their current state is too many vibes and very little actual advice on what to describe. I may be wrong, but Ramnesis has not commented for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T07:32:26-07:00","id":1562260,"title":"","content":"The first and primary reason for the thread is to look at the game reasons, game balance or thematic or otherwise, for the Otherworlds being described the way they currently are. Then, in light of those reasons, look at ways of reworking Otherworlds travel to eliminate the various contradictions and special pleading that Mage is full of.<br /> <br /> The Penumbra has taken center stage because of how the Vidare Mortem works with the Shadowlands, or more accurately, how it doesn\u2019t. It makes for a very good example and poster child, but there are other issues too.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming Penumbra is a lesser issue because we can reasonably go either way. Mage is explicit that the Underworld is an Umbra (or part of the greater Umbra). It says no such thing about the Dreaming. Now it is rather easy to view the Dreaming as an Umbra in its own right because it has that broadly similar structure that runs from largely earthlike and even mapping to the physical world on one end, to increasingly divorced/rarified as you get farther out. We can push it into that mold, but we are not obligated to like we are with the Underworld. Dreaming travel itself is important, but we can consider that whether there is a Dreaming Penumbra or not.<br /> <br /> As an aside, even when I do consider a Dreaming Penumbra I don\u2019t think of it as a reliable way of getting to the rest of the Dreaming. It would be by far the rarest to have a connection with the physical and the hardest to find from the rest of the Penumbra. I think entering through dreams and demenses would be the preferred method.<br /> <br /> Following up on one other thing, if the Penumbra is an interstitial or liminal space between realms, it would make sense that there are frequencies of it beyond the big three. It also means something doesn\u2019t have to be an Umbra for the Penumbra to touch upon it. In fact it would open the possibility that the Astral, Wilds, and Underworld are fundamentally different things that happen to touch on the same space. I still like that idea, though it is just one possible view. However, it is also worth noting that even if it is such a space, it isn\u2019t the only one. The Midrealm and Mount Qaf are both said to touch upon many other realms. It isn\u2019t necessary that all of them touch upon everything with the same level of ease.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T11:13:34-07:00","id":1562266,"title":"","content":"In fact, both things could be true: a Chimerical perception perceives things that are in the Material, but made of pure Glamour, and there could also exist a Dream Penumbra.<br /> <br /> And I find this idea interesting because it both closes possible structural gaps but expands our avenues for mystery and exploration.<br /> <br /> We don't invent rules to make it fit what the Fae perceive and know. Instead it is its own thing, and the Fae aren't even aware of its existence. Maybe they can sometimes notice hints, but no different from Sleepers noticing hints of other Penumbrae. It may have unknown spirits and/or Chimeras, its own phenomena, its own links to other parts of the Dreaming or to Dreams. It could, by its proximity yet distinction from the Material, house phenomena the games still don't have.<br /> <br /> Stuff that get shunt from reality due to Paradox or Banality could end up here, alongside echoes of the time when it happened. A liminal space that receives Bygones, Marauders and Chimeras before they wander, though some may stay.<br /> <br /> Now, a single Penumbra for both the Dreaming and the Dream Zone, for only one of them, or both? I don't think we need answers for this, but is good food for thought.<br /> <br /> Personally I think it should connect to the Dream Zone only if it has clear connections to the Dreams, but that brings the next can of worms:<br /> <br /> Do other Realms have Penumbrae? Are they complete? What is it like to be in an Umbra proper and not in a Realm, is that even a thing? Or is the Penumbra also the space between realities? If so, what it looks like to wander the Penumbra between Realms rather than in 3 dimensions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T08:28:19-07:00","id":1562560,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the Dreaming has interactions outside of what the Fae and other glamour aligned creatures know. The Otherworlds often are bigger than any one group can see, even one that is closely intertwined with them.<br /> <br /> Whether other Realms (and here I'm using that term for the broad Realms, not the individual realms within them) have Penumbrae is going to depend a great deal on what Penumbrae are. I think in this thread we've seen a few general possibilities.<br /> <br /> 1) The Penumbra is a transitory zone between the physical and multiple Otherworlds. Because of the interaction of those Otherworlds it can take on the flavor or frequency of them.<br /> <br /> 2) Each Penumbra is an interface between the physical and another Otherworld. For various metaphysical reasons it is often possible to move from one Penumbra to a different Penumbra associated with the same physical location.<br /> <br /> 3) The Penumbra is an interstitial space between multiple Otherworlds. A location in the Penumbra frequently takes on elements from the closest Worlds to it. One of these locations is almost always the Physical, which is why it usually looks like a shadow of the physical. Whether or not that's an actual metaphysical rule is unclear.<br /> <br /> Those are very broad strokes and I could easily make the list longer just by subdividing them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T09:21:20-07:00","id":1562651,"title":"","content":"One of the things that complicates the Otherworlds is the methods of travel, because they are bit strange, particularly the big three (Stepping Sideways, Astral Projection, and Out of Body Experience aka The Agama Sojourn). If I had to hazard a guess why, it\u2019s because they are a mix of bringing in elements from other game lines, protecting other game lines, and replicating real world practices.<br /> <br /> For the big three, each one corresponds to one of the three main Umbras, though they are not always exclusive to them.<br /> <br /> <b>Stepping Sideways</b> means piercing the Gauntlet and stepping to the other side, transforming from a physical body to a spiritual one or back depending on the direction. Despite the change, mechanically the body uses largely the same rules. This is the method that leans towards the spiritual, but it is also the generic method. A spiritual body will function in the Penumbra, the lower reaches of the Astral, and all of the Spirit Wilds.<br /> <br /> This is the simplest method, in terms of Sphere cost, at Spirit 3 (or 4 for others).<br /> <br /> Much like the Middle Umbra this one seems to be largely a port from Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Astral Projection</b> means projecting the mind from the body to float around on its own, though still connected by a silver cord. This body is largely ephemeral and does not interact with the physical. This method leans towards the mental/Astral but it is not limited to that and doesn\u2019t even have to be a form of Otherworlds travel at all. It can float about the physical, the Penumbra, and the Astral as well as project into other things, like objects, people, and dreams. A mage can build himself a spiritual body to project into, though, which will let him traverse the Spirit Wilds as well.<br /> <br /> Astral Projection alone requires slightly more training than Stepping Sideways, at Mind 4 (or 5 for others). Building a spiritual body requires Spirit 3/Prime 2 (plus Mind 4(5) to project into it).<br /> <br /> This one is the most Mage specific.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>OBE</b> means bringing the body to a state of near death or suspended animation, allowing the soul to project directly to the Shadowlands as a ghost. This body is very much like that of a wraith. This method leans the most towards the Underworldly.<br /> <br /> The reason I\u2019m calling it OBE rather than the Agama Sojourn is that Mage, for some strange reason, assumes the only reason anyone would want to do this is Chakravanti Initiation. Considering there are enough other reasons to be the basis of an entire WoD game line, Orpheus, that\u2019s a strange assumption.<br /> <br /> This is the most stringent method, coming in at Entropy 4/Spirit 3/Life 2(3), and its the one I'm most inclined to change. There\u2019s not an explanation for Entropy I\u2019d suggest dropping it entirely. In light of Orpheus Sleepers, I\u2019d also consider letting Life 2(3) alone let a mage make the initial projection into the Shadowlands, but any subsequent Shroud/Gauntlet crossings would still take Spirit 3. <br /> <br /> I can't know the minds of the authors, but it seems like this one was set up begrudgingly. It is in many ways a port from Wraith, but with the decision to make it very rare and difficult. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If we drop M20s Schrodinger\u2019s Penumbra approach to the Shadowlands and just say they are Penumbral, that would mean that the Astral and Spiritual bodies can visit at least the Shadowlands, while ghostly bodies can visit the rest of the Penumbra. There is no guidance for how far the former can get into the Underworld or how far the latter can get elsewhere.<br /> I can actually think of some novel uses to adapt these more broadly, but that\u2019s for another time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are other methods of Otherworlds travel, though I largely don\u2019t think they have the same kind of problems. The main two I can think of are:<br /> <br /> <b>Realm Specific Methods.</b> This covers travel to specific Otherworlds based on their themes and metaphysics. Access to the Digital Web falls into this category, as would accessing the Dream Zone through a demenses. I think there are some realms within the larger high and middle umbras that can be accessed this way, but I don\u2019t recall for certain.<br /> <br /> <b>Extant Gateways and Portals.</b> Previously set up portals can take a mage just about anywhere, including to any of the Otherworlds. These could be naturally occurring Shallowings, or Gateways created by long dead mages, or moon bridges, or anything. They could require specific actions to open, or key spells, or anything. These are largely dictated by the narrative rather than any system. This can include the gateways into Horizon Realms (though that might also fall under Realm Specific Methods).<br /> <br /> I may be missing some others, but I think that covers most of it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T10:58:40-07:00","id":1562665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be missing some others, but I think that covers most of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are also spells that basically allow you to enter places where you normaly need OBE, w/o the Out of Body part. If I remember correctly the VE have a Rote that it's basically Agama, but with Life 4 and it allows to enter the Shadowlands bodily. VA can enter the Web &quot;Holistically&quot; also with Life (or with normal Stepping Sideways by first taking a detour trough the Cyberrealm) <hr /><br /> For the purpose of this houserule set, I would argue Spirit should be all you need to go anywhere. Those complications can be replaced with the whole idea of shifting your frequency.<br /> <br /> The other ways to travel have the advantage of protecting your body (OBE, Astral, Virtual gadgets - it's hard to trully *kill* you on the other worlds with any of these) and/or that the magick it's already worked out (Portals). Balance wise it's ok if they're a bit more limited to where they take you, but can be &quot;upgraded&quot; with Spirit for the full dimensional experience<br /> <br /> Maybe some places require further magick, but not necessaily different methods. Nephilim allows you to use Mind 4 / Spirit 3 (for...reasons) to travel to the High Umbra <i>bodily</i> - presumably to all of it, or it would be a hefty tax on doing somehting anyone can do with Spirit 3 and a little climbing. This is <i>harder</i> than Spirit 3, but it's not very <i>different</i>. It's just a very expensive <i>gate</i> that needs a special bloodline + a Mind-key to <i>unlock</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we drop M20s Schrodinger\u2019s Penumbra approach to the Shadowlands and just say they are Penumbral, that would mean that the Astral and Spiritual bodies can visit at least the Shadowlands, while ghostly bodies can visit the rest of the Penumbra. There is no guidance for how far the former can get into the Underworld or how far the latter can get elsewhere. </div> </div> </div>The real limitation about traveling further into the Underworld isn't the method of entering (OBE, OBE w/o the O, Stepping Sideways with the Merit that allows you to go there), but rather than to travel further one needs to be able to open Nihils and traverse the Tempest. Wraiths can do this with Argos (and some Wraiths could take a Mage alongside with them), but there's little data about doing similar effects with Magic(k) - I think there was ONE mention on the Book of Worlds on a table (and it was ludicrously hard, like Entropy 5 hard), but I don't have BoW at hand to check.<br /> <br /> I don't see why Magic(k) should have a limitation about this, tho. In the Lore mages *do* in fact go further. In the BoW a mage *talks* about places further, and let's not forget that Wraith gameline was ended partialy by a mage droping a nuke into Oblivion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-04-2026, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T13:06:29-07:00","id":1562680,"title":"","content":"First a correction: Astral Projection was ported from Vampire, even if there is no mention to other realms, but is where the idea of being immaterial in the material enters WoD.<br /> <br /> As for missing methods, you left out the Paths of Wyrd, that seem to let you travel without any Magic if you know the labyrinthine steps, but may also be just a very weird Instrument.<br /> <br /> That aside, for the methods I agree with Aleph that using Spirit as an all-purpose baseline and then explore others as tradeoff alternatives with less reach is ideal. In a sense you're robbing Spirit of its whole shtick if you say an otherworld is off-limits to the Sphere of otherworlds.<br /> <br /> What I would do:<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Stepping Sideways</b></i></u> - go to an &quot;adjacent&quot; realm. As a rule of thumb that's the Penumbra, but certain places can offer stranger options. The rule of Frequency applies and is built in the Sphere.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Astral Projection</b></i></u> - leave the body behind, has the benefits and drawbacks associated. You can start your journey at mind-oriented places or as a disembodied mind in the Material. You can start your journey in the Astral if you want, the Dream Zone or the Dreaming depending on where you are, or the respective Penumbra frequencies. This converts your astral body into an actual local body, but the silver cord remains. You can use other available methods as usual to travel further, or repeat the spell to change the mental Realm you're in.<br /> <br /> <i>Greatest advantage</i>: your body is where you left it, and you can at any time Magic your way to your own mind, though this may not be much safe if you don't have a Demense. That's a safe-ish travel.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>OBE</b></i></u> - It deposits you in a death-related Realm, which includes, but isn't limited to, the Underworld. This is essentially your disembodied soul, which makes it Wraith like and even susceptible to the same rules. You can use other Magics to travel to other Realms, but you can't repeat the spell during your travels, so brace yourself to danger.<br /> <br /> <i>Particulars of this</i>:<br /> <br /> 1. You're not limited to collocation, your arrival can happen at any point of a Death Realm you are familiar with, without extra Spheres.<br /> <br /> 2. Body behind is a slight protection. Having your soul body destroyed can have all sorts of repercussions, but will generally wake you in your body with whatever they are. Having your soul trapped, though, is another story.<br /> <br /> 3. Probably an easier time with Effects that a Wraith could do without much XP, at least. For a lot of effects you can pass for one or Magic yourself into imitating one with ease.<br /> <br /> 4. I'd seriously consider lowering requirements but making it dangerous. Putting yourself in a near death state isn't without risk, not only of dying in case something goes wrong and your body don't get help, but of coming back with some consequence of the physical side of the experience.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Paths of Wyrd</b></i></u> - at baseline do not require any Magic. If you do find a true Path, it's just a matter of following it and dropping wherever in the way you want. Maps for those Paths exist, but errors can't be retraced, if you step out and leave the Path at some point, going back isn't just a matter of going back, at each point the entering has a proper method. You're traveling bodily, so take care.<br /> <br /> <i>Particulars of this</i>:<br /> <br /> 1. All sorts of Magic can interact with the Paths of Wyrd or guide you through them. You can use Corresponce to find them, map them or manipulate them, you can use Entropy to avoid leaving the Path or even finding a &quot;good&quot; one without knowing or mapping it.<br /> <br /> 2. Paths are locked. You don't control where you go in any special way.<br /> <br /> 3. Paths are potentially dangerous as they have environment, travelers and inhabitants. Since this can be quite a roundabout journey, that's not a small thing.<br /> <br /> 4. Time is wonky in a Path, each in its own way. Outside that, they're also quite long to walk.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Transition Zones</b></i></u> - several, maybe infinite &quot;all-touching&quot; realities exist. Those places connect to other worlds in particular points, and internally follow their own spatial logic. A castle full of doors that deposit you elsewhere with no way back. A seemingly infinite staircase in a void where each landing has a door that does exist in the other side. A giant World Tree where branches do follow some structure you can follow, but guarded by strange inhabitants. A misty expanse where time doesn't exist, full of portals you can only have a rough idea where they'll deposit you.<br /> <br /> <i>Particulars of this</i>:<br /> <br /> 1. Each Transition Zone has its own entry and exit rules. Some can be accessed with ease by anyone, some even by accident, while others require special Magics.<br /> <br /> 2. They can be explored more or less freely, as wandering around won't kick you out (usually).<br /> <br /> 3. Distance between exit and entry points are unpredictable, though most are faster than a Path of Wyrd.<br /> <br /> 4. To find one of those you can use Spirit, though it's usually necessary to know what you're looking for, as they have their own Frequencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T14:07:29-07:00","id":1562689,"title":"","content":"I wasn\u2019t specifically thinking about Paths of the Wyrd. I did consider Transition Zones, though, I just didn\u2019t enumerate them. Realms like that have their own specific entry and exit rules which falls under Realm Specific Methods. I didn't flesh those out too much, though I may come back to it later.<br /> <br /> In regards to the utility of Stepping Sideways, I didn\u2019t try to curtail its range. Mage locked that form out of the higher reaches of the Astral. Same for the Underworld, though we are discussing fixing that one.<br /> <br /> That said, I\u2019m not completely on board with it being the baseline. It might be the most comfortable or versatile, but I\u2019d rather lean into the three as fundamentally different approaches with advantages and disadvantages.<br /> <br /> I do think projection and OBE should be better at navigating the Astral and Underworld respectively. That doesn\u2019t have to be handled by locking other forms out of those areas, though.<br /> <br /> This is what I see as the major advantages and disadvantages of each method.<br /> <br /> <b>Stepping Sideways</b><br /> Advantages<ul><li>You mostly have the body you are used to (its made of spirit but it feels and functions mostly the same)</li> <li>You can cross back over anywhere; you don\u2019t have to return to a body</li> <li>This form is the best at navigating the Spirit Wilds</li> <li>This form is potentially the most versatile or functional of the forms when it comes to working outside its ideal World</li> <li>You can bring things with you without issue</li> </ul>Disadvantages<ul><li>You mostly have the body you are used to</li> <li>There\u2019s no quick way back or emergency escape</li> <li>If you are trapped, you have to deal with acclimation</li> <li>The cost of death is death</li> </ul><br /> <b>Astral Projection</b><br /> Advantages<ul><li>This form is naturally capable of flight</li> <li>This form can operate in the physical world</li> <li>This form has direct and quick access to large areas of the Astral</li> <li>This method can bypass the gauntlet difficulty (I think)</li> <li>This method has an easy form of return (by the silver cord)</li> <li>This form is the best at navigating the Astral</li> <li>The cost of death is going adrift</li> </ul>Disadvantages<ul><li>This form loses access to physical traits</li> <li>This form has a vulnerability in the form of the silver cord</li> <li>This form has difficulty interacting in more physical realms</li> <li>You have to return to the point you started from</li> <li>The physical body is left vulnerable</li> <li>Being adrift means a limited amount of time to find your way back before death</li> </ul><br /> <b>OBE</b><br /> <i>A lot depends on details of how the spell works. Going with a version where you automatically manifest in the Shadowlands, and if the spell ends you snap back if you can...</i><br /> Advantages<ul><li>The ghost body is potentially the most durable form</li> <li>The ghost form may be able to cross back over and operate in the physical world</li> <li>OBEs bypass the difficulty of the local gauntlet/shroud</li> <li>This form has direct access to the Shadowlands</li> <li>Return is automatic if the spell ends</li> <li>This form is the best at navigating the Underworld</li> <li>This form can potentially pass as that of a normal ghost</li> <li>The cost of death is harrowings</li> </ul>Disadvantages<ul><li>This form has some interaction with the Physical world even from the Shadowlands</li> <li>This form is subject to harrowings and long term damage from them</li> <li>You have to return to the point you started from</li> <li>The physical body is left very vulnerable</li> </ul>Since part of this is hashing out how OBE should work, this is all subject to change.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T15:43:20-07:00","id":1562696,"title":"","content":"I think this approach for now has two problems in the concept, not execution:<br /> <br /> 1. Astral Projection and OBE are things that exist in real life occult and have actual cultural practices. Stepping Sideways is a holdover from Werewolf. Actual shamanic journeys are more linked to trances of drug use, with the same effect of the body being left behind. It changes more in the sense that its felt as an embodied experience, as if the shaman inhabits a spiritual form that's solid there.<br /> <br /> 2. We lack rules on how those forms would be able to traverse between Realms and Umbrae, except for Stepping Sideways, so even without being called baseline, in practice it is.<br /> <br /> Also we have to think about Sphere requirement, and I feel that if the other two get to travel everywhere in some way, they'd have to also include Spirit. And if they don't, but can use Spirit, we face the problem of a Form using another Form. It's also possible that they don't require, but adding Spirit changes some of their properties, but them I don't know yet what to make.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it now, I do think a Shaman Form is a must have, and Stepping Sideways shouldn't actually be a regular Mage feat \u2013 a possible feat, but one very few know and use. Even the mirror version of it in real folklore is actually linked to mirrored water surfaces, not to solid mirrors (and could maybe be a way to OBE into the Dreaming).<br /> <br /> As for the rules:<br /> <br /> Stepping Sideways has the problem of collocation: you cross to the equivalent space and only to a neighboring realm.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of Astral and OBE bypassing the Gauntlet if they don't have Spirit as a requirement and don't travel out of their respective turf by Magic.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I like your versions, but we need to think what &quot;best at navigating&quot; means, and if it is a general rule (and easy to transpose to new Umbrae and Forms) or a per form property.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T07:18:34-07:00","id":1562724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562696#post1562696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this approach for now has two problems in the concept, not execution:<br /> <br /> 1. Astral Projection and OBE are things that exist in real life occult and have actual cultural practices. Stepping Sideways is a holdover from Werewolf. Actual shamanic journeys are more linked to trances of drug use, with the same effect of the body being left behind. It changes more in the sense that its felt as an embodied experience, as if the shaman inhabits a spiritual form that's solid there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and that's what I was talking about earlier when I said they were a mix of other game line elements and real world occult ideas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. We lack rules on how those forms would be able to traverse between Realms and Umbrae, except for Stepping Sideways, so even without being called baseline, in practice it is.<br /> <br /> Also we have to think about Sphere requirement, and I feel that if the other two get to travel everywhere in some way, they'd have to also include Spirit. And if they don't, but can use Spirit, we face the problem of a Form using another Form. It's also possible that they don't require, but adding Spirit changes some of their properties, but them I don't know yet what to make.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it now, I do think a Shaman Form is a must have, and Stepping Sideways shouldn't actually be a regular Mage feat \u2013 a possible feat, but one very few know and use. Even the mirror version of it in real folklore is actually linked to mirrored water surfaces, not to solid mirrors (and could maybe be a way to OBE into the Dreaming). </div> </div> </div>There's another complication, but it's only partly in stepping sideways. The easiest way to illustrate it is a question: what does Stepping Sideways actually do? Does it transfer someone across the Gauntlet AND transform their body into a spiritual one? Or does it just transfer them across the Gauntlet and that transformation just naturally happens to anyone who moves from the physical to the spiritual?<br /> <br /> I say that it is a complication not limited to stepping sideways because there are other ways people can stumble into the Umbra, like Shallowings. If the intention was that sometimes this wouldn't transform the person, I'd expect to see some handling of what that would look like. On the other hand, maybe no one considered it, or there wasn't the word count. Whichever way we take this, it affects more than just Stepping Sideways. This is a metaphysical element underlying some Otherworlds travel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the rules:<br /> <br /> Stepping Sideways has the problem of collocation: you cross to the equivalent space and only to a neighboring realm.<br /> <br /> I'm in favor of Astral and OBE bypassing the Gauntlet if they don't have Spirit as a requirement and don't travel out of their respective turf by Magic. </div> </div> </div>I'd add that they likely still cross the Gauntlet enough to interact with the Avatar Storm, if it is in play. However the thickness of it doesn't appear to hinder them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise I like your versions, but we need to think what &quot;best at navigating&quot; means, and if it is a general rule (and easy to transpose to new Umbrae and Forms) or a per form property. </div> </div> </div>I agree. I prefer the best at navigating to the hard limits and additional Spheres that Mage uses. Restrictions should be more a matter of challenges. If a spirit body can't get to the higher reaches of the Astral, why not? If it has more difficulty dealing with the Tempest, what does that look like?<br /> <br /> It's not that blanket restrictions don't work. If the three Umbrae are actually each their own thing it would make sense that they play badly with metaphysics outside their own. But those restrictions should still have some metaphysical reason behind them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have some indication of what the Astral Body challenges are. It lacks physicality. Even in the Otherworlds where it is not as intangible as it is in the physical, the mage still uses mental and social attributes in place of physical ones, indicating a fundamental change. Places it has difficulty with should challenge that in some way. An Astral body could be far more easily blown about by Tempest winds than other forms, for instance. While I don't see anything universal in the Spirit Wilds, many of the individual realms there have physical properties rather than just being ephemeral. An Astral Body would function there much like it does in the physical world, which could be a hindrance or a blessing depending on the realm. That leaves the Labyrinth. I don't yet have an idea for the problems an Astral Body would face there.<br /> <br /> The Ghost Body has similar problems to the Astral Body in the Spirit Wilds: it doesn't change into a physical form when it crosses into a physical realm. The same realms that the Astral Body can't interact with, the Ghost Body will be semi-ephemeral in. Only in this case the mage can't fly and the Rule of Ouch likely applies. Again, I think that's a reasonable basis to say that it has problems in the Spirit Wilds.<br /> <br /> I still can't think of a problem the Ghost Body would have with navigating the Astral. Mage makes it sound like the mage would need to project an Astral Body from his Ghost body to go there, but if a mage in an Astral Body of Light can travel there, I don't think having a kind of physicality is the problem.<br /> <br /> I'm really not sure what to do with the Spiritual Body though. It likely has whatever challenges the Ghost body has in the Astral, but as above, I'm not sure what those are. Meanwhile I don't see any real metaphysical problem with a Spirit Body in the Tempest or Labyrinth. I do think that actual wraiths and spectres would instantly recognize that a Spirit Body is not a ghost, so it could be that it is the inhabitants that make the Underworld so dangerous, but I find that generally unsatisfying. <br /> <br /> I'll keep thinking about it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T08:12:39-07:00","id":1562727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd add that they likely still cross the Gauntlet enough to interact with the Avatar Storm, if it is in play. However the thickness of it doesn't appear to hinder them.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Infinite Tappestry Astral travel was introduced as one way to bypass the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> I think having ways to bypass the Storm trough knowing it's metaphisics it's more interesting than just saying &quot;pay for the Merit&quot; or &quot;you can't&quot;. If you know the Storm affects the Gauntlet but not more, say, &quot;natural&quot; ways to travel, I say it's ok to reward that knowledge - coupled with the magical power to take advantage of it - with safe travel. Within the limitations of said travel methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T08:26:48-07:00","id":1562731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562727#post1562727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On Infinite Tappestry Astral travel was introduced as one way to bypass the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> I think having ways to bypass the Storm trough knowing it's metaphisics it's more interesting than just saying &quot;pay for the Merit&quot; or &quot;you can't&quot;. If you know the Storm affects the Gauntlet but not more, say, &quot;natural&quot; ways to travel, I say it's ok to reward that knowledge - coupled with the magical power to take advantage of it - with safe travel. Within the limitations of said travel methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had thought that Astral Travel was explicitly not a way to get around it, but it's admittedly been a while since I read Revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T09:16:05-07:00","id":1562734,"title":"","content":"The &quot;material constitution&quot; part is a heavy conundrum. Even the other forms have this. Spirits are made of ephemera, but there's something else in the Astral Body, what? And the Underworld is not made of ephemera, its made plasm IIRC (never read Wraith much). A stuff Wraiths can mold, something they can't with ephemera. How does this interaction work?<br /> <br /> I think the flesh-ephemera translation would be more satisfying as a property of the spell, and have rules for flesh-ephemera interactions. We know from spirit incursions that ephemera can interact with mater, but it requires charms.<br /> <br /> My first thoughts: mater doesn't chemically interact with ephemera, even when it physically does. And that means you can't breath or feed in the Umbra without some intervention. Granted, many methods may include intervention or translation, but isn't a given. Also, Adaptation takes hold at least 4\u00d7 faster.<br /> <br /> What may make things easier is the abstract, semantic nature of ephemera. Despite not having chemical interactions, an ephemeral object still affect your metabolism as a charm like property. The air in inhabited areas keep you alive because that's what air does there. If an object is conceptually food, it will feed you. But the key here is that exceptions may happen due to non obvious reasons. The air above the city is breathable way beyond where it should ratify. The air in some places may have no notion of a human breathing, even if it is technically normal air.<br /> <br /> The constitution factor is the reason the Astral Body is immaterial and flies everywhere, it's not composed of ephemera or actually anything but thoughts. But the Astral does interact with thoughts as physical actions.<br /> <br /> What about the ghostly one? First question: how do Wraiths interact with other worlds, including the material? Do they actually cross to the material?<br /> <br /> How they Astral behave in the Astral Realm? First I think it still fly, which is a big help ascending the Spires. Second it csn freely interact with or ignore anything, as they're pure thought. I think the Astral Umbra shouldn't be made of ephemera, even if most inhabitants are. It's made of some other concept material that interact to your thoughts, only, following what you believe or should do. Other forms have a harder time with the Spirals.<br /> <br /> For me the bigger problem with the Astral is that only the Spires are described in a way that makes going there easy to describe and play. The Vulgate definitely should have more about it, and fuck you Epiphanies. The Astral Body could be better with those if they had more explanations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T11:47:04-07:00","id":1562740,"title":"","content":"Well it certainly looks to me like Spirit 3 has the capability of turning the physical into the ephemeral and vice versa, so it is certainly possible that is a part of Stepping Sideways.<br /> <br /> Actually, your breakdown of how the physical and ephemeral interact raises the possibility that Stepping Sideways doesn't convert the mage at all. It goes against what Mage says, but what would be damaged if that were true?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The ghost questions depend greatly on if we are talking Wraith or Orpheus.<br /> <br /> In Wraith, interaction with other worlds is exceptionally limited. There's not much to determine how wraiths would interact with the ephemeral or astral, though there is some indication of some greater entities like Anubis that might be able to enter and exit the Underworld. Anubis could also just be a very old wraith, though.<br /> <br /> As for the physical, yes Wraiths can cross the Shroud in short bursts. There are a number of Arcanoi that interact with the physical world, some by manipulating it across the Shroud and a few by actually crossing and manifesting or possessing something. But because these powers are all meant to do something specific in the physical, we don't get much indication of what a wraith just being in the physical would by like. It might be like a permanent form of Embody, or it might be something else.<br /> <br /> Orpheus increases the ease of that, but also it might give us an indication of what ghosts in the physical world are like.<br /> <br /> Now without getting into the weeds, it is possible that ghosts in Orpheus are still operating out of the Shadowlands and nothing has changed. On the other hand, it is possible that the 6th Great Maelstrom pushed into the Shroud making the nigh impassable Stormwall, and ghosts are now operating out of the Physical. If that is true, it would indicate that ghosts in the physical exist in an intangible state unless they choose to manifest or interact.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that while Sleepers project by going into cryostasis, Skimmers project by meditation and their method has a lot in common with astral projection, including the silver cord. Orpheus really wasn't concerned with interaction with other game lines, so we should be careful about taking too much from that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As a last thought, I'm not sure there actually is a difference between plasm and ephemera other than verbiage. I mean on first glance it is easy to think they are different, but they could also just be different arrangements of the same substance. I suppose it most depends on if we want the three Umbra to be composed of the same or different substances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T12:36:45-07:00","id":1562741,"title":"","content":"My take on Stepping Sideways is that it's literally what it's OoC: a take from Werewolf, as in Kinfolk Mages developed it based in what Garou do. Garou are part spirit and naturally convert to Ephemera, while using them as basis resulted in the same despite crossing and translating being independent level 3 effects. Maybe not exactly independent, as in this case the way the Mage is traversing the Gauntlet may be using the properties of ephemera. Meaning it's a &quot;low cost&quot; process. If we go for that, Stepping Sideways without a translation to Ephemera may require a few extra successes, making it so bad that few Mages with Spirit 3 know or care about it.<br /> <br /> We can then put a Shamanic-style journey in Spirit 2, but it would be more constrained as the other two are.<br /> <br /> AFAIK everyone in the Underworld is solid to the Underworld, and Wraiths are solid for each other in the Shadowlands. If this is indeed the case I'd say it resembles more living flesh in the other Umbrae rather than being intangible, being solid but with interaction facing challenges unless the local Ephemera or their Plasm have the right individual rules.<br /> <br /> I take this also from the fact that many of the big players in the Underworld are not Wraiths and may not be made of Plasm, including spirits, Angels, Mummies, Mages, Vampires... Whether that's true is immaterial, there wouldn't be a doubt if solidity were a giveaway.<br /> <br /> Being different materials is also not as big a factor, a &quot;different arrangement&quot; would still be enough to change interaction, maybe even be impossible to determine with known methods. The fact that some difference exist is enough to give us freedom to define how they behave. I'm in favor of they being at least partially different, though, because it would be interesting for there to be some doubt if the Material we know is really as unique/central as we think, or if it is just another Umbra to the Umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-05T14:12:30-07:00","id":1562751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562724#post1562724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another complication, but it's only partly in stepping sideways. The easiest way to illustrate it is a question: what does Stepping Sideways actually do? Does it transfer someone across the Gauntlet AND transform their body into a spiritual one? Or does it just transfer them across the Gauntlet and that transformation just naturally happens to anyone who moves from the physical to the spiritual?<br /> <br /> I say that it is a complication not limited to stepping sideways because there are other ways people can stumble into the Umbra, like Shallowings. If the intention was that sometimes this wouldn't transform the person, I'd expect to see some handling of what that would look like. On the other hand, maybe no one considered it, or there wasn't the word count. Whichever way we take this, it affects more than just Stepping Sideways. This is a metaphysical element underlying some Otherworlds travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall any written rules that answers these questions, so I'm just going to put on a Dimensional Scientist Hat and write down my stream of thought:<br /> <br /> We can think of umbral realms as reality zones with their own rules and metaphysics, and a traveler has to exist in them in a compatible manner or the realm would reject them. Compatible being the keyword, because the nature of the ephemeral body does not change to that of the natives of the realm - a Wraith is different from a Spirit or a Chimera, and an Astral Projection is different from a body that has stepped sideways. They all have different qualities, even in the form of OoC rules.<br /> <br /> Going with the frequency analogy, stepping sideways into an umbral realm means adjusting the frequency of the body to that of the realm. I'm going to stretch the analogy by saying it's like moving the dial on a radio and leaving the base frequency until you find the carrier wave you're looking for. A Penumbra would be the space between the signals where you catch the sidebands of both. In Star Trek they would say you're going out of phase, but let's stick with frequency. Essentially, stepping sideways changes the body into a state that is compatible without changing its nature. This would also cover Shallowings and Paths of the Wyrd, as they would be like turning the dial with a different method.<br /> <br /> But that leaves OoB and Astral Projection (and shamanic journeys or other separations of consciousness): They appear like those frequencies attunements exist within oneself and can be separated to journey instead. Extrapolating from that, maybe we can think of the Material as the white noise of overlapping frequencies, and those methods would work like a filter instead of attunement.<br /> <br /> In other words, stepping sideways is an adjustive process (change the frequency), and AP/OoB are substractive (filter the noise). <br /> <br /> --<br /> Ok, that came out more rambling than I thought, but maybe there is something useful in there. The idea of the Material as the 'white noise' of umbral frequencies can maybe explain some interactions between the realms that bypass the normal mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T07:11:02-07:00","id":1562773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562731#post1562731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had thought that Astral Travel was explicitly not a way to get around it, but it's admittedly been a while since I read Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the ways to avert the storm. I checked it, p. 16 of The Infinite Tappestry (on the wings of tought): &quot;The primary advantage of this form, obviously, it's that it completely bypasses the Avatar Storm, since the body is not physically present in the transit...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not obvious at all ... but knowing it works like this one could extrapolate and think that similar forms of travel would also bypass the Storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  It was needless 08-06-2026, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T10:20:11-07:00","id":1562777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562741#post1562741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on Stepping Sideways is that it's literally what it's OoC: a take from Werewolf, as in Kinfolk Mages developed it based in what Garou do. Garou are part spirit and naturally convert to Ephemera, while using them as basis resulted in the same despite crossing and translating being independent level 3 effects. Maybe not exactly independent, as in this case the way the Mage is traversing the Gauntlet may be using the properties of ephemera. Meaning it's a &quot;low cost&quot; process. If we go for that, Stepping Sideways without a translation to Ephemera may require a few extra successes, making it so bad that few Mages with Spirit 3 know or care about it.<br /> <br /> We can then put a Shamanic-style journey in Spirit 2, but it would be more constrained as the other two are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting thought. My initial thought is that this might work by creating or awakening a sort of spirit representation of the mage with a specific purview and spirit stats based on the number of successes rolled. I'm also inclined to say that since Spirit 2 doesn't normally have that degree of ephemera manipulation, this would require Prime 2s Body of Light as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562741#post1562741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK everyone in the Underworld is solid to the Underworld, and Wraiths are solid for each other in the Shadowlands. If this is indeed the case I'd say it resembles more living flesh in the other Umbrae rather than being intangible, being solid but with interaction facing challenges unless the local Ephemera or their Plasm have the right individual rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes that is a different behavior between spirits and ghosts, and there are a number of those, like that ghosts naturally don\u2019t fly or float without arcanoi while apparently spirits naturally do,* spirits have appearances that shift with the viewer while ghosts do not, etc.<br /> <br /> *I actually never really thought of spirits that way, I always considered them to move in whatever made sense for the type of spirit they were.<br /> <br /> However, I quickly realized that a lot of that can be traced to different origins. Because a wraith was once a living human, he brings elements in that are not present in spirits. For instance, he brings in his own expectations about his appearance, which shapes how he appears. That\u2019s actually explicit in Wraith, their appearance is based on how they feel they should appear. Beneath the surface the difference is actually a similarity. <br /> <br /> There are a number of other elements like this. Both are heavily dependent on a core idea; the wraith\u2019s core idea is the person they were in life. Their passions and fetters are all built around that. Both slumber in a place associated with their nature to recover their health/power track, and again for wraiths that place is a fetter which is based on who they were in life. There are some more obvious similarities too, such as the way they both react when they run through their health/power track. Both dissipate or are otherwise pulled away and reform later.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say the biggest difference that is left is the completely different stats, with wraiths using a standard WoD stats spread while spirits use the Werewolf WP/Rage/Gnosis/Essence port. This could still be because different origin points, but its not as clear that it is. It could also just be that Mage simply ported the respective systems from WW and Wraith and there\u2019s no deeper meaning. Hard to say.<br /> <br /> Strangely, there\u2019s no system difference between spirits of the Astral and spirits of the Spirit Wilds. Possibly that\u2019s just because there was nowhere to port the astral from so no outside rules to follow. Possibly that\u2019s because there\u2019s a fundamental difference between ghosts and spirits and that would most likely be either origin or the fact that ghosts are souls not spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562741#post1562741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being different materials is also not as big a factor, a &quot;different arrangement&quot; would still be enough to change interaction, maybe even be impossible to determine with known methods. The fact that some difference exist is enough to give us freedom to define how they behave. I'm in favor of they being at least partially different, though, because it would be interesting for there to be some doubt if the Material we know is really as unique/central as we think, or if it is just another Umbra to the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d actually prefer they be quite different as well, because the things they represent don\u2019t have any real reason to be connected. I think I\u2019d prefer separate realms rather than the Material being one of the Umbra. Or possibly, the Material is one of a number of realms that act as that special fulcrum point. That would work too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562751#post1562751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going with the frequency analogy, stepping sideways into an umbral realm means adjusting the frequency of the body to that of the realm. I'm going to stretch the analogy by saying it's like moving the dial on a radio and leaving the base frequency until you find the carrier wave you're looking for. A Penumbra would be the space between the signals where you catch the sidebands of both. In Star Trek they would say you're going out of phase, but let's stick with frequency. Essentially, stepping sideways changes the body into a state that is compatible without changing its nature. This would also cover Shallowings and Paths of the Wyrd, as they would be like turning the dial with a different method.<br /> <br /> But that leaves OoB and Astral Projection (and shamanic journeys or other separations of consciousness): They appear like those frequencies attunements exist within oneself and can be separated to journey instead. Extrapolating from that, maybe we can think of the Material as the white noise of overlapping frequencies, and those methods would work like a filter instead of attunement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that an unmoored mind automatically has compatible frequencies with the Astral and an unmoored soul automatically has compatible frequencies with the Underworld, as that is a large part of what those Worlds are.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, there really isn\u2019t anything like that for the Spirit Wilds. As far as I know there isn\u2019t an unmoored part of a person that naturally gravitates that way. The mage doesn\u2019t become a spirit or in any way take on the abilities of a spirit, he more just turns himself into a version of himself made out of ephemera.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps he turns himself into a spirit with the specific and perfect purview of \u2018himself,\u2019 which binds him into acting exactly like he would act. I can see some mages viewing it that way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T11:56:02-07:00","id":1562781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562773#post1562773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one of the ways to avert the storm. I checked it, p. 16 of The Infinite Tappestry (on the wings of tought): &quot;The primary advantage of this form, obviously, it's that it completely bypasses the Avatar Storm, since the body is not physically present in the transit...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not obvious at all ... but knowing it works like this one could extrapolate and think that similar forms of travel would also bypass the Storm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not obvious at all. But MRev never mentions the storm or the gauntlet in the section about Astral Projection, so I guess it was intentional. The other thing that's odd is I thought one of the major points of the Avatar Storm was to push Mage more towards the street level. That's actually why I assumed the Astral was cut off too. Guess not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T14:21:17-07:00","id":1562791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562777#post1562777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely, there\u2019s no system difference between spirits of the Astral and spirits of the Spirit Wilds. Possibly that\u2019s just because there was nowhere to port the astral from so no outside rules to follow. Possibly that\u2019s because there\u2019s a fundamental difference between ghosts and spirits and that would most likely be either origin or the fact that ghosts are souls not spirits.<br /> [...]<br /> Oddly enough, there really isn\u2019t anything like that for the Spirit Wilds. As far as I know there isn\u2019t an unmoored part of a person that naturally gravitates that way. The mage doesn\u2019t become a spirit or in any way take on the abilities of a spirit, he more just turns himself into a version of himself made out of ephemera.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is the astral was designed as analogue to the Middle Umbra for Mages to play in. There was no distinction necessary, so rules for inhabitants and travel could just be copied.<br /> At the same time, I don't think introducing such differences would hurt or change the worldbuilding too much, since the two were made to be independent of each other anyway.<br /> <br /> I've been looking up umbral travel in <i>Spirit Ways</i>, and the default of shamans seems to be Dreamwalking / Astral Projection / Mind 4 into the Spirit Wilds as opposed to the Astral, either while sleeping, with drugs, or by sensory deprivation. That's at least a good indicator such an unmoored part of a person exists, it just shares a name with that of the Astral.<br /> <br /> Interesting side note is that the Time 2 divinatory effects are listed there under the Umbral Travel section. It's very certainly a Paradigm thing but the idea of past and future as umbral directions is intriguing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T22:12:34-07:00","id":1562815,"title":"","content":"WoD uses the concept of many souls, or many aspects of them soul, regularly, so I think a j\u00e9 ne sais quoi inside the Mage that attunes with the Middle Umbra, or even made of Ephemera, is perfectly possible. It's not the same thing as a Wraith, but is just as much part of the Mage.<br /> <br /> I'd use this to keep it Spirit 2 as an effect. I think the &quot;OoB Forms&quot; could rely much more in magicking the aspect of the Mage out to the Umbra rather than a complex transportation, so they can be relatively low Sphere. I'd use the stats of the Mage to create a baseline for the Shamanic Body, and then only increase it if the Mage has, in fact, Spirit 3+.<br /> <br /> My take would be then that those &quot;soul bodies&quot; are limited to the realms they appear in until they find natural passages. The Astral is made of Abstraction, the Shamanic is Ephemera and the Ghostly is Plasm.<br /> <br /> Other parts of the soul may correspond to other Umbrae, like something made of Glamour for the Dreaming. Also, given the intangibility of the Astral and the rules for navigation in the Astral Umbra, I think it's actually made of nothing, just a disembodied mind. My theory is that the Astral is directed by pure thought, and being free of embodiment the Astral form is free of embodied expectations. But in theory anyone can do anything in the Astral Umbra if they can literally put their minds into it.<br /> <br /> As for the spirits of the Astral, my guess at first is that many aren't actually native to it. If they are, they may be just as intangible as the Astral form, it's just that without leaving the realm of thought-based interaction this is meaningless in practice, you'd have to bring them out to be sure.<br /> <br /> Curiously Glamour entities also have their own rules, and even the Chimeras use a full stat block. So that deepens the mystery: Ghosts and Fae use complete stats and proper rules, which is both a similarity and a distinction in those rules. Spirits do use identical rules. Uhm, maybe we're fundamentally wrong about what the Astral IS, and instead it is closer to the Middle Umbra than it appears at first.<br /> <br /> There is something in common among them: they're concepts given form. That's not how Ghosts or Fae work. Ghosts are self images, but also once formed something about them is ontologically fixed, it is regardless of anyone's ideas. Fae are the same, be it Gallain, Kithain or Chimera, they're born from imagination and Glamour, but once they are their reality is fixed regardless of what others think. Spirits, though, most are concepts, ideas about things, and they react to changes in collective perception for whatever group that matters. More powerful ones seem to be more resistant, but that may be just due to resistance. Or maybe they do change and retroactively remember as always being.<br /> <br /> Yes, either some connection between Spirit Wilds and Astral exist, or there's a cause for a similarity that's enough for them to use the same rules despite being ontologically distinct. We also have a strange and interesting case to analyze: the Djinn. They're objectively different from other spirits in some degree, despite the use of the same rules, and everything points to them really being native to the Material, or at least being way more comfortable there than other spirits. They built citadels in the High Umbra, but can and do travel all over the Umbrae and their Realms, can live anywhere no problem, have no need for anything special to live close to or within the Material, even living as humans sometimes.<br /> <br /> So we have actually three types of entities that follow the same rules, but also seem to be fundamentally distinct, all using the same Essence substance, Spirits from the Wilds, the Astral Spirits and the Djinn. What could be a common factor to justify their rules, even if as convergence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-07T05:35:14-07:00","id":1562826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1562815#post1562815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be a common factor to justify their rules, even if as convergence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Doylist I think it's just a convenience. The Astral and Djinn don't have their own games so they don't have their own separate rules. <hr /><br /> Lorewise, I think it could be justified by the deeply mythical but very much constant references to a past where these realities were one. Be it from Werewolf, Demon or even Mage to some extent, there are references to a time where things were both concepts given form by their concept, and distinct material substance - the separation of the spritual and the material it's an artificial happenstance.<br /> <br /> That being the case, the rules are given by the force that yanked the two appart, and some beings can &quot;slip trough the cracks&quot; by rejecting this transformation, so to speak. The mage &quot;remembers&quot; this state of being a concept, the Djinn (that also have dynamic magick even if not always represented by Spheres) are the same but in reverse.<br /> <br /> The Astral represents a version of things containing it's abstract representations. Cities are represented as highly developped places because they're built on engineering, maths, science - rather than looking as their more vivencial Spirit Wilds counterpart that takes more in count HOW people and living things live there. Both may be conceptual, but one it's more like watching a schematic combined with a sociological study (that may contain zones of &quot;suffering&quot; in the slums, that are conceptualized as bad places. That may contain places of high religiosity and piety on churches and similar) and the other it's more emotionaly connected with the world.<br /> <br /> Since the Astral can be accessed from the Spirit by climbing the Webs of the Weaver, it's likely this sepparation it's likewise, artificial. But it's meaningful enough that some spirits just can't access both. The Triad influence it's much more tenuous, with only the Weaver having significative presence - and even then there aren't that many Weaver-specific Astral spirits. Garou are naturally rejected to the point the whole World it's hostile to them (according to the most recent book, I don't remember well, but I think it had something to do with their Rage not being healty there).<br /> <br /> The Underworld was either sepparated from Creation from the get go, or maybe at an earlier stage compared to the other two big worlds. Maybe the Dreaming too.<br /> <br /> Ultimately everything starts to coalesce as &quot;one&quot; on the Deep Umbra beyond the Solar System, when you go outside of the Telluriam itself and start flirting with the idea of whole alien cosmologies existing beyond our own. Tho interestingly, no one in the Underworld has managed to reach the stars <i>and returned to tell the tale (</i>not the same as saying it's impossible) <hr /><br /> Realy powerful or primordial entities like &quot;high end&quot; gods and demons that have their own Realms can bridge the gap between the worlds, existing in several at once. And not just between the Astral and their Middle Umbra counterparts - some also have a connection with the Underworld Far Realms (such as it's the case of Hela's Nilfheim - and if Hela's Astral Realm can have a connection there, then why not Hell and Heaven?).<br /> <br /> You can travel between the Worlds by finding these connections - wich it's one of the canon ways a Mage can find themselves <i>deep</i> into the Underworl. It enters on the same category as <b>Realm Specific Methods </b>- but I bring it up because the entities that rules these interactions also seem to exist in many realms at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":".  corrections 08-07-2026, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T09:38:18-07:00","id":1563009,"title":"","content":"I do think the Doylist answer for the similarity of rules is the predominant reason. We may be able to use the common rules to derive a small amount of information; it shows there is enough conceptual similarity to use the same rules. But I don\u2019t think that we can go beyond that to derive much about their substance or metaphysics.<br /> <br /> After all, If we only had the setting from Wraith but not the rules, I suspect Mage would default to the standard spirit rules for ghosts, but I don\u2019t think that would change anything about what ghosts are.<br /> <br /> Going back to the question of if ephemera and plasm are the same thing? That's going to depend a lot on how the worlds relate to each other. But since that's something mages in universe would argue about and we have reason to keep that kind of argument going, I think we have to choose the answer that leaves the most room while having the easiest rule set. So I think my general approach would be: there is a difference between the two that can be determined by some senses or with some examination, but both fall under the purview of Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T11:49:44-07:00","id":1563015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559478-game-reasons-for-the-different-types-of-umbral-travel?p=1563009#post1563009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going back to the question of if ephemera and plasm are the same thing? That's going to depend a lot on how the worlds relate to each other. But since that's something mages in universe would argue about and we have reason to keep that kind of argument going, I think we have to choose the answer that leaves the most room while having the easiest rule set. So I think my general approach would be: there is a difference between the two that can be determined by some senses or with some examination, but both fall under the purview of Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree. I tend to see the rules of Spirits as an abstraction anyway, mostly because the WTA stats Rage and Gnosis make only sense for a part of them... even in WTA. Why would a Weaver Spirit have Rage? Why do Astral Spirits have Gnosis?<br /> <br /> My suggestion:<br /> If you abstract the WTA values to, say, Agency and Energy you could flavor a Spirit or other Ephemeral to fit their role and habitat. Their Energy and Agency defines how their Essence is expressed.<br /> <br /> So for example, a book standard Spirit would have an Essence of Gnosis and Rage which is called &quot;Ephemera&quot;. A Plasmic has an Essence of Angst/Passion and Pathos which is called &quot;Plasm&quot;. <br /> <br /> Astral Spirits could have an Essence of &quot;Aether&quot;, as a function of Reason and Quintessence. Some more exotic types could work with Sekhem, Chi, or Glamour.<br /> You could even describe inanimate Ephemera variants like that if you say they don't have Agency and Willpower.<br /> <br /> The specifics aren't really important in most cases, but removing/changing the WTA attributes allows for more flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}